# sprint/schema-c takes sprint/schema-go: the C base forward-merge

THE TASK. sprint/schema-c is about 686 commits behind sprint/schema-go (64dc1ddd when carded; GO TIP below is the tip you fetch, at or after it). Merge origin/sprint/schema-go into the base as ONE merge commit on the card branch: git fetch origin, then git merge --no-ff GO TIP. Never a rebase, never a squash, never a force-push. A trial merge on 2026-10-18 left these conflicts (a newer GO TIP may add a few; resolve those by the same rules): ROADMAP.md, internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go. Resolve each conflict keeping BOTH sides' intent, by these rules and no others: shared Go and IR code (ir/, internal/check/, internal/parser/, compiler/, internal/codegen/gotable/, tools/, .github/) takes GO TIP's version; port-specific code keeps the port's version, adapted to the new IR; spec text (docs/*.md) merges both rewrites, each statement true of the merged code; ROADMAP.md is regenerated with make roadmap, never hand-edited; the roadmap sexp ledgers (docs/roadmap.sexp, docs/roadmap-evidence/*.sexp) keep each row's true state at the merge head. internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go: the C base threads a `depth` argument into fixedLoopVar, GO TIP carries a g.fixedLoop counter and emitFixedWriteArm. Keep one fixedLoopVar and one counter scheme, the one GO TIP's emitFixedWriteArm calls, keep the C base's behaviour, and keep every caller compiling; the C fixed-form tests in internal/codegen/ctable are the judge. Then regenerate the goldens, the generated trees and the bench the merge leaves stale with the repository's own Makefile targets, and commit the regenerated files in the merge commit or a second commit on the same branch. Nothing else changes: no rule is ported here.

LANDING. The card lands by pushing the merge to the base: the head is the merge commit (plus any regeneration commit), the member pushes the branch, and nova-sprint land brings it onto sprint/schema-c with the merge commit kept, never squashed or rebased.

DONE-WHEN: git merge-base --is-ancestor GO TIP HEAD is true at head and false at BASE (print both and the GO TIP hash); git log --merges -1 --format=%P HEAD names BASE's tip and GO TIP; the port's unit gate (go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/, then make generated-current) passes, with no new reds against the pre-merge BASE except reds that are also red on GO TIP itself, each named and shown red there (TestSpecGoS13S15FollowOnsLanded is one of those).

ROUTE NOTE (coordinator, 2026-10-19). Start from the CARRY head: its source is ready (attempt 7 merged the attempt-6 carry with Go 0c9a03a3, restored compiler/tablescwire_test.go to the Go tip blob and kept the C fixed-form work byte-identical). Gates are owed: try up to three least-loaded Linux benches before holding. Before finishing: (1) re-merge the CURRENT origin/sprint/schema-go tip (at this note 50a2372589e4, newer than 0c9a03a3) into the head; (2) docs/roadmap.sexp gets a true three-way merge of both parents, never one side copied; then run make roadmap so ROADMAP.md is the tool's output of the merged ledger, and make roadmap-check green; (3) regenerate the stale golden/generated/bench trees with the tools only; (4) run GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/ and make generated-current at base, at the Go tip and at the final head, keeping the raw output. Merge-carried files equal to the merged parent or to the merge-tree result are granted. An inherited red (for example TestCTableWireBlobIdentity at the Go tip) is reported with its Go-tip line, never fixed by copying from an unlanded card. Name the merged schema-go sha and the final head sha in the report.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Run the gate at BASE first and keep each last line (go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/, then make generated-current): those are the pre-merge reds.
STEP 3. git fetch origin; print GO TIP (git rev-parse origin/sprint/schema-go); git merge --no-ff GO TIP; list the conflicts with git diff --name-only --diff-filter=U and resolve each by the rules in THE TASK. Commit the merge with the trailer.
STEP 4. Regenerate (make roadmap, then each stale golden, generated tree and bench) and run the gate. When a test fails, name its file and say whether it was changed by your resolution (yours), arrived red from schema-go (run it at GO TIP and keep the line), or is unchanged (already red at BASE), and report that line first.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against the BASE: line's branch, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the merge commit, each conflict and how it was resolved, the diff stat against BASE, the gate lines, and what was not done.
STEP 6. End as JOB.md says; the report starts with Verdict: LAND or Verdict: HOLD on line 1 and Head: <sha> on line 2.")
