# C: one blob record named from two slots is blob_shared: writers refuse it, the tolerant read keeps one node and counts it, the strict read refuses it

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (c-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §2.5 and §16.7: every writer refuses a graph whose two slots name one blob (by name, blob_shared, never a bare -1); the tolerant Load keeps the ONE node (never a copy per slot) and counts the extra slots in report.blob_shared; the strict read refuses blob_shared; the message form's region writer and reader take the same ruling. Add the blob_shared counter to TableReport and the paths in internal/codegen/ctable/graph.go,internal/codegen/ctable/blobs.go,internal/codegen/ctable/pointers.go,internal/codegen/ctable/message_graph.go. Files: internal/codegen/ctable/graph.go,internal/codegen/ctable/blobs.go,internal/codegen/ctable/pointers.go,internal/codegen/ctable/message_graph.go, the generated trees.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 is the answer key, and it is on this base after the forward merge: internal/codegen/gotable/blobnamedtwice_test.go (TestBlobNamedTwiceSeed24's wire, TestBlobNamedTwiceWriters, TestBlobNamedTwiceAmplification's 4096 slots on one 64 KiB blob, TestBlobNamedTwiceMessageForm). Every expected answer the new test asserts is the one that Go test pins for the same schema text and the same input bytes, transcribed into the C probe with a comment citing the Go file and the case; never a value this port computed for itself. Read the Go emitter beside it (internal/codegen/gotable, named in the citation) for the rule's edges before writing the C one.

THE GAP AT BASE. grep -n 'blob_shared\\|BLOB_SHARED' internal/codegen/ctable/*.go prints nothing at BASE.

Do not edit docs/SPEC-TABLES.md or docs/USAGE.md: where this card makes a backend-status sentence there stale (\"Go is first and the only target\", \"every other target refuses\"), quote the sentence and the one-line replacement in the pull request as a proposed diff for the spec helper.

DONE-WHEN: go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./compiler/ -run 'TestCBlobNamedTwice' fails at BASE (its failing assertion, kept from STEP 2) and passes at head; go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/, then make generated-current and make tables-c are green or their only reds are named as present at BASE; the grep in THE GAP AT BASE no longer shows the gap at head.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Red first: TestCBlobNamedTwice in compiler/cblobshared_test.go, opening with t.Parallel(), built with compileAndRunC (compiler/tabledeadc_test.go) or runCTableWireProbe (compiler/tablescwire_test.go) for a compiler-level probe, cRunSelfBuilt (internal/codegen/ctable/fixedroadmap_t06_test.go) for a fixed-form probe; run it at BASE and keep the failing line (`no tests to run` before the file exists is not the red: write the file, then run it and keep its failing assertion).
STEP 3. Make it pass in the files PATHS names, citing the SPEC section (and the Go oracle file) from each emitter function that implements the rule. Regenerate every generated tree the change moves with its own Makefile stamp target until make generated-current passes, and commit the regenerated files.
STEP 4. Run the gate: go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/, then make generated-current and make tables-c, and read the last line of each. When a test fails, name its file and say whether that file was changed by your work (yours) or is unchanged (already red at BASE: run the same test on the unchanged base to say so), and report that line first.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against the BASE: line's branch, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, what was deleted, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
STEP 6. End as JOB.md says: where JOB.md ends the card with its pull request, that is the end and there is nothing else to write, the gate's lines in the pull request body; where it asks for RESULT.md, write it in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report).")
