# C: text lists `[N]string(M)`, `[E]string(M)` and `[..N]string(M)` / `[..N]?string(M)` are carried

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (c-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §2.13: a text list is an array whose element is text, bounded per element by M and in count by N. refuseTextForms (compiler/tablesstringarrays.go (read) after the forward merge) refuses every text list for every target but go. Carry the BOUNDED spellings for \"c\" on every form the port has (variable wire, message form, fixed form for the fixed-size spellings, JSON, the view descriptor), each element held to M and the count to N as Go holds them, then make refuseTextForms let \"c\" through for the bounded text list alone (unbounded text, the array root and `| total` stay refused: their cards follow) and update TestStringArraysRefusedOffGo's bounded rows to exclude \"c\". Files: internal/codegen/ctable/sequence.go,internal/codegen/ctable/text.go,internal/codegen/ctable/wire_read.go,internal/codegen/ctable/codecs.go,internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go,internal/codegen/ctable/json.go,internal/codegen/ctable/view.go,internal/codegen/ctable/ctable.go, compiler/tables*.go, the generated trees.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 is the answer key, and it is on this base after the forward merge: internal/codegen/gotable/stringarrays_test.go TestGoTableStringArraysAndJSONArrayRoot (its text-list rows: the wire bytes, the JSON text and the clamp of an over-long element). Every expected answer the new test asserts is the one that Go test pins for the same schema text and the same input bytes, transcribed into the C probe with a comment citing the Go file and the case; never a value this port computed for itself. Read the Go emitter beside it (internal/codegen/gotable, named in the citation) for the rule's edges before writing the C one.

THE GAP AT BASE. refuseTextForms in compiler/tablesstringarrays.go (after the forward merge) refuses `[..N]string(M)` for \"c\".

