THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §16.11: testgen writes, per unit file with a root table, a generated test of a value through the three forms (binary, base64, JSON) and back and of a damaged input refused by name; a table whose forms leave out wire or json is refused by name at testgen. compiler/testgen_go.go (read) (after the forward merge) refuses every target but go. Add the C testgen (a NEW emitter file beside ctable), written against the generated C API and the language's standard library only, run by a make target as the port's other generated tests are, and let c through compiler.Testgen; TestTestgenIsGoOnly changes to the targets that carry it. Files: internal/codegen/ctable/testgen.go (new), compiler/compiler.go (read), compiler/generate.go (read), the make file the port's tests live in, the generated trees.

