# C: SaveText and LoadText, canonical base64 of the binary wire, LoadText strict

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (c-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §16.8: EVERY TABLE HAS BOTH text carriers, and the C port has the JSON one only. Emit SaveText and LoadText for every root (C spells each name in the port's own snake_case form (`<root>_load`, `<root>_load_tolerant`, the claimed-suffix row of docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §11 spelled as `<name>_fixed_save` is spelled)): SaveText writes the canonical base64 (standard alphabet, padded, pad bits zero, no whitespace) of exactly the bytes Save writes; LoadText decodes and reads with the plain strict Load (a fixed root: a value filled by Load; a variable root: its own builder and the locked root, as ReadStrict does), refusing whenever the report holds an error. A text that, with its CR and LF dropped, is padded standard base64 that decodes but is not the canonical encoding of those bytes refuses base64_not_canonical; every other failure (a byte outside the alphabet and `=`, a missing, extra or misplaced `=`, a text that does not decode) refuses base64_damaged; a decoded wire the binary read refuses is that read's own refusal. report is optional; a supplied one receives this read's report. No allocation on the fixed path beyond what Load has; claim both suffixes in internal/tablenames/c.go. Files: internal/codegen/ctable/text.go,internal/codegen/ctable/ctable.go, internal/tablenames/c.go, the generated trees.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 is the answer key, and it is on this base after the forward merge: internal/codegen/gotable/base64canonical_test.go TestGoLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 (its pad-bit, inner `=`, whitespace, CR/LF and wrong-padding rows and their names) and the SaveText/LoadText round trips of internal/codegen/gotable/unboundeddescriptor_test.go. Every expected answer the new test asserts is the one that Go test pins for the same schema text and the same input bytes, transcribed into the C probe with a comment citing the Go file and the case; never a value this port computed for itself. Read the Go emitter beside it (internal/codegen/gotable, named in the citation) for the rule's edges before writing the C one.

THE GAP AT BASE. grep -n 'SaveText\\|save_text\\|LoadText\\|load_text' internal/codegen/ctable/*.go prints nothing at BASE.

Do not edit docs/SPEC-TABLES.md or docs/USAGE.md: where this card makes a backend-status sentence there stale (\"Go is first and the only target\", \"every other target refuses\"), quote the sentence and the one-line replacement in the pull request as a proposed diff for the spec helper. Bytes fields inside JSON (schema-go-json-base64-canonical) are still WORKING on schema-go and are NOT this card.

DONE-WHEN: go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./compiler/ -run 'TestCLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64' fails at BASE (its failing assertion, kept from STEP 2) and passes at head; LoadText(SaveText(v)) is byte for byte Save(v) for every root of the bench corpus unit the probe generates; go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/, then make generated-current and make tables-c are green or their only reds are named as present at BASE; the grep in THE GAP AT BASE no longer shows the gap at head.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Red first: TestCLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 in compiler/cbase64carrier_test.go, opening with t.Parallel(), built with compileAndRunC (compiler/tabledeadc_test.go) or runCTableWireProbe (compiler/tablescwire_test.go) for a compiler-level probe, cRunSelfBuilt (internal/codegen/ctable/fixedroadmap_t06_test.go) for a fixed-form probe; run it at BASE and keep the failing line (`no tests to run` before the file exists is not the red: write the file, then run it and keep its failing assertion).
STEP 3. Make it pass in the files PATHS names, citing the SPEC section (and the Go oracle file) from each emitter function that implements the rule. Regenerate every generated tree the change moves with its own Makefile stamp target until make generated-current passes, and commit the regenerated files.
