# C: `?map[K]V` is carried, absent, present-empty and present-with-entries three values

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (c-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §2.8: an optional map carries a present companion, and ABSENT, PRESENT-EMPTY and PRESENT-WITH-ENTRIES are three values on the wire (absent writes nothing; present-empty writes the field header and the two-byte array body `0d 00` under L = 2), in JSON (absent omits the key, present-empty is `{}`, null reads absent), through retain-unknown and the cook, with the descriptor naming the field optional and its present offset; a reader built without the `?` reads the three silently as plain maps. refuseOptionalMaps (compiler/tablesmaps.go (read)) refuses it for every target but go. Carry it for \"c\", then take \"c\" out of refuseOptionalMaps and TestMapPresenceRefusedOffGo. Files: internal/codegen/ctable/maps.go,internal/codegen/ctable/wire_read.go,internal/codegen/ctable/json.go,internal/codegen/ctable/view.go,internal/codegen/ctable/retain_emit.go,internal/codegen/ctable/cook.go, compiler/tablesmaps.go (read), the generated trees.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 is the answer key, and it is on this base after the forward merge: internal/codegen/gotable/mappresence_test.go TestGoMapPresence (the pinned wire bytes of each of the three values and the JSON of each). Every expected answer the new test asserts is the one that Go test pins for the same schema text and the same input bytes, transcribed into the C probe with a comment citing the Go file and the case; never a value this port computed for itself. Read the Go emitter beside it (internal/codegen/gotable, named in the citation) for the rule's edges before writing the C one.

