# C: FixedLoad and LoadMessages are strict by their plain names; FixedLoadTolerant and LoadMessagesTolerant are the named twins

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (c-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §6.5, the same bullet as the plain binary Load, for the two other binary reads: FixedLoad answers -1 and LoadMessages answers ok == false (count 0 when the strict rule alone refused, the tolerant count otherwise) on a read that is clamped, kind-mismatched or malformed; on that refusal FixedLoad resets every value it wrote and LoadMessages resets every value it wrote when the strict rule alone refused (records ahead of a body the tolerant read itself stopped on keep what they decoded). FixedLoadTolerant and LoadMessagesTolerant carry exactly BASE's signatures and answers. Callers in test/c-tables/**,test/conformance/c/**,bench/tables/c/** that relied on the tolerant answer move to the Tolerant name. Files: internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go,internal/codegen/ctable/fixedruntime.go,internal/codegen/ctable/message_read.go,internal/codegen/ctable/message.go, internal/tablenames/c.go, the generated trees.

