# C: timestamp text is strict RFC 3339 section 5.6 date-time, and \"c\" leaves the central timestamp refusal

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (c-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §2.11 and §16.2 (7fb89e941): a timestamp's JSON text is exactly RFC 3339 §5.6 `date-time`, and anything else refuses the read by name, timestamp_not_rfc3339. Implement the strict parser and the writer in the C text form (internal/codegen/ctable/json.go,internal/codegen/ctable/graph_json.go) to the rule internal/rfc3339 implements in Go (read it; do not call it: the generated C carries its own), then take \"c\" out of the timestamp branch of compiler/generate.go (read) (line 99 after the forward merge) and out of the refusal's test, leaving every other non-Go target refused. Files: internal/codegen/ctable/json.go,internal/codegen/ctable/graph_json.go, compiler/generate.go (read), the generated trees.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 is the answer key, and it is on this base after the forward merge: internal/rfc3339/rfc3339_test.go TestStrictRFC3339 (every accepted and refused spelling) and internal/codegen/gotable/timestampstrict_test.go TestGoTimestampStrictRFC3339. Every expected answer the new test asserts is the one that Go test pins for the same schema text and the same input bytes, transcribed into the C probe with a comment citing the Go file and the case; never a value this port computed for itself. Read the Go emitter beside it (internal/codegen/gotable, named in the citation) for the rule's edges before writing the C one.

THE GAP AT BASE. compiler/generate.go line 99 refuses every unit holding a timestamp for \"c\".

Do not edit docs/SPEC-TABLES.md or docs/USAGE.md: where this card makes a backend-status sentence there stale (\"Go is first and the only target\", \"every other target refuses\"), quote the sentence and the one-line replacement in the pull request as a proposed diff for the spec helper. THE CARRY REGISTRATION (coordinator rule 2026-10-18): the central refusal is lifted for \"c\" by registering the target as a carrier of this construct in compiler/target_c.go, the per-target declaration file schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries defines (if that card's landing names another per-target file, use that one and say so in the pull request); never by editing compiler/generate.go or a shared refusal list, and the construct's TestXRefusedOffGo test then reads the carrier set, so \"c\" drops out of it with no edit to its lines.

