STEP 2. Red first: TestCTimestampTextStrictRFC3339 in compiler/ctimestamptext_test.go, opening with t.Parallel(), built with compileAndRunC (compiler/tabledeadc_test.go) or runCTableWireProbe (compiler/tablescwire_test.go) for a compiler-level probe, cRunSelfBuilt (internal/codegen/ctable/fixedroadmap_t06_test.go) for a fixed-form probe; run it at BASE and keep the failing line (`no tests to run` before the file exists is not the red: write the file, then run it and keep its failing assertion).
STEP 3. Make it pass in the files PATHS names, citing the SPEC section (and the Go oracle file) from each emitter function that implements the rule. Regenerate every generated tree the change moves with its own Makefile stamp target until make generated-current passes, and commit the regenerated files.
