# C++: `?T` whose T holds a pointer is carried, every pointer walk gated on presence

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (cpp-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C++ port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §2.3: a `?T` over a VARIABLE closure (T, or something T reaches, holds a pointer) gates every walk that follows pointer edges on the presence companion: Measure, Save, the node numbering, Lock, the cook, retain and the JSON writer never follow an edge an absent value does not own. compiler/generate.go (read) refuses it for every target but go (the TableOptionalPointerClosures branch, line 136 after the forward merge). Carry it for \"cpp\", then take \"cpp\" out of that branch and of TestOptionalVariableRefusedOffGo. Files: internal/codegen/cpptable/pointers.go,internal/codegen/cpptable/arena.go,internal/codegen/cpptable/json.go,internal/codegen/cpptable/retain.go,internal/codegen/cpptable/cook.go, compiler/generate.go (read), the generated trees.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 is the answer key, and it is on this base after the forward merge: internal/codegen/gotable/optionalvariable_test.go TestGoOptionalVariableClosureTable. Every expected answer the new test asserts is the one that Go test pins for the same schema text and the same input bytes, transcribed into the C++ probe with a comment citing the Go file and the case; never a value this port computed for itself. Read the Go emitter beside it (internal/codegen/gotable, named in the citation) for the rule's edges before writing the C++ one.

THE GAP AT BASE. compiler/generate.go line 136 refuses `?T` over a variable closure for \"cpp\".

