# C++ and C: a deprecated enum variant reads as the field default and is refused on write

RULING (Glenn, 2026-10-18): \"If it's possible to implement, then implement it!\" Enum variants may be deprecated in place (`| deprecated`), one way only. The standard (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md, card spec-enum-variant-deprecated-in-place) and the Go reference (cards schema-go-enum-variant-deprecated-front-end and schema-go-enum-variant-deprecated-codegen) define it; this port matches Go.

PRECONDITION. The front end (parser, ir Variant.Deprecated, check, lock) is shared and lands on sprint/schema-go. If BASE's ir has no Variant.Deprecated, stop at once with Verdict: HOLD, not-done naming the forward-merge of sprint/schema-go into sprint/schema-cpp that is owed; write nothing.

NOTE: start from the port base after cpp-base-forward-merge-schema-go lands. Do NOT carry head 2da9ae1f: it holds its own merge of sprint/schema-go outside PATHS.
THE TASK. In the C++ and C table emitter and runtime: a reader meeting a deprecated variant's id, on every form this port carries (id-table wire, form 3, message form, JSON/text where carried), yields the field's declared default (elements: the element default) and does not count unknown; every writer this port has refuses a value holding a deprecated variant with invalid_value, naming <Table>.<field>; the variant's constant stays, marked deprecated in the language's idiom.

TEST, opening with t.Parallel(), under the port's house pattern (a generated unit run in a t.TempDir()): TestDeprecatedVariantReadsDefaultWriteRefused: a wire written with the variant live reads the default once it is deprecated; each writer refuses; REVERSED WITNESS: the same wire read with the variant live yields the variant. Where Go's reference test gives bytes, this port's reads agree with them.

DONE-WHEN: the test RUNs and PASSes at head (red at BASE: no tests to run) for every form the port carries, with its reversed witness; the port's gate passes or its only reds are named as red at BASE.

