# C++: a plain float's -0, NaN and infinities take one rule in every form

PORT TO THE STANDARD (Glenn 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages.\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as they stand on this base after the forward merge (cpp-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f, which brings mas-bandwidth/schema sprint/schema-go at d808c3f54); schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. This card is one feature of the C++ port and nothing else.

THE TASK. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) §3.3, \"A PLAIN FLOAT'S SPECIAL VALUES TAKE ONE RULE\": the default elision compares BIT PATTERNS, so -0 rides the variable and message forms rather than eliding to +0 and the text reads -0 as -0; a NaN or an infinity rides the binary forms bit for bit, the tolerant read names it non_finite in the report's reason and counts nothing, and the strict read refuses it with non_finite (the TableRefuseReason value the reason-enum card appended), because the JSON writer has no spelling for it. Make the C++ emitter's elision tests bitwise and add the non_finite path. Files: internal/codegen/cpptable/codecs.go,internal/codegen/cpptable/messagecodec.go,internal/codegen/cpptable/messageload.go,internal/codegen/cpptable/json.go, the generated trees.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 is the answer key, and it is on this base after the forward merge: internal/codegen/gotable/floatspecial_test.go TestGoPlainFloatSpecialValuesAgreeAcrossForms (fsSchema, fsFlatSchema, fsKeyedSchema; every assertion on the raw bits). Every expected answer the new test asserts is the one that Go test pins for the same schema text and the same input bytes, transcribed into the C++ probe with a comment citing the Go file and the case; never a value this port computed for itself. Read the Go emitter beside it (internal/codegen/gotable, named in the citation) for the rule's edges before writing the C++ one.

THE GAP AT BASE. grep -n 'non_finite\\|NON_FINITE' internal/codegen/cpptable/*.go prints nothing at BASE.

Do not edit docs/SPEC-TABLES.md or docs/USAGE.md: where this card makes a backend-status sentence there stale (\"Go is first and the only target\", \"every other target refuses\"), quote the sentence and the one-line replacement in the pull request as a proposed diff for the spec helper.

