# C# carries the `timestamp` kind (kind 36) on every binary form

The standard's current wording (§2.11) has Go carry `timestamp` first and every other target refuse it by name until its own turn, so for C# the family is \"carry timestamp\": the wire first, the strict RFC 3339 text in the next card.

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.11 (storage, kind 36, the wire bytes). Oracle: TestTimestampKindInGo and its pinned wire bytes at d808c3f54.

THE GAP (read at BASE, after the forward merge). compiler/generate.go at BASE answers cs with `the cs target does not carry the timestamp kind`.

THE TASK. Register cs as a timestamp carrier and carry the kind through the C# storage, the variable, message and fixed forms, the cook and the view as Go does, the wire bytes equal to Go's.

CARRYING A GO-FIRST CONSTRUCT. At BASE the compiler refuses this construct for target \"cs\" by name (the central refusal named under THE GAP). After schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries (schema-go; it arrives with the forward merge) a target declares what it carries in a file of its own: add the NEW compiler file this card names, one init() calling registerCarried(\"cs\", \"<construct>\") (compiler/carries.go) with the construct this card carries, and a test in compiler/ where c.Generate of the refusal test's own probe unit for target cs answers files and no error while every other non-Go target still refuses it by the same name. Never edit compiler/target_cs.go, compiler/generate.go or compiler/carries.go here.

THE TESTS. The new test lives in the NEW file named above, in package cstable, and drives generated C# the way internal/codegen/cstable/messageform_held_test.go does (csDotnetToolchain: Roslyn csc plus dotnet exec, one build, one run): it generates the probe unit with the compiler, compiles it with a C# probe program, runs it and parses its lines. THE EXPECTED ANSWERS COME FROM SCHEMA-GO at d808c3f54: copy the oracle test's schema and its pinned bytes, reasons and values (the oracle is named under THE RULE), never a value worked out by hand; where the Go oracle prints wire bytes, the C# leg must print the same bytes. The dotnet-driven test skips by name without dotnet and fails by name under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1, as its neighbours do. Add no make target (make/cs.mk is not in PATHS): the test runs under go test ./internal/codegen/cstable/.

