# C# plain Load, region Load and LoadBuilder are strict; the tolerant read keeps a name of its own; ReadStrict and Report.Err arrive

schema-go made the plain read name strict (schema-go-strict-read-by-default; commits 61105d0b1, 1f53ff49d, f995112ac, bcff9c99e, 2c0700baa). The C# leg has no strict read at all: its plain Load is tolerant and there is no ReadStrict, no Tolerant twin and no typed reason on the report.

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5 (\"The STRICT read\" and \"THE PLAIN NAME IS THE STRICT READ; THE TOLERANT READ HAS A NAME OF ITS OWN\") and §11. Oracle: TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict (internal/codegen/gotable) and the TableRefuseReason enum and TableReport.Err in internal/codegen/gotable/refusal.go at d808c3f54.

THE GAP (read at BASE, after the forward merge). `grep -c ReadStrict internal/codegen/cstable/*.go` is 0 at BASE; the C# TableRefuseReason (cstable.go, the line beginning `public enum TableRefuseReason`) has no malformed, clamped, kind_mismatch, wire_damaged, invalid_value, allocation_failed, base64_damaged, base64_not_canonical, integrity_mismatch, non_finite or blob_shared, all of which Go's enum carries.

THE TASK. (1) Append Go's values the C# enum lacks to TableRefuseReason in Go's order and spelling (never renumber an existing value): invalid_value, allocation_failed, wire_damaged, malformed, clamped, kind_mismatch, base64_damaged, base64_not_canonical, integrity_mismatch, non_finite, blob_shared; this card owns the whole enum line so the later C# cards only use names. (2) Add TableReport.Err() answering Go's order of checks (refused/unknown form, integrity_mismatch, wire_damaged, missing_required, malformed, blob_shared, clamped, kind_mismatch, non_finite) and null on a clean read or one whose only counters are unknown, widened or retained, carried the C# way (a typed exception class TableRefusedException holding the reason, returned rather than thrown by Err()). (3) Emit <Name>ReadStrict(bytes, out reason) for each root. (4) Make the plain <Name>Load (value), the region <Name>Load and <Name>LoadBuilder strict as §6.5 says (same signatures, the report overwritten with this read's report, the refusal value false or a null root, the value reset to its defaults on refusal), and emit <Name>LoadTolerant and <Name>LoadBuilderTolerant with the old behaviour. FromJson, FixedLoad and LoadMessages are the three cards that depend on this one; leave them alone. Re-pin goldens that change (testdata/ is in PATHS) and update callers in tests.

THE TESTS. The new test lives in the NEW file named above, in package cstable, and drives generated C# the way internal/codegen/cstable/messageform_held_test.go does (csDotnetToolchain: Roslyn csc plus dotnet exec, one build, one run): it generates the probe unit with the compiler, compiles it with a C# probe program, runs it and parses its lines. THE EXPECTED ANSWERS COME FROM SCHEMA-GO at d808c3f54: copy the oracle test's schema and its pinned bytes, reasons and values (the oracle is named under THE RULE), never a value worked out by hand; where the Go oracle prints wire bytes, the C# leg must print the same bytes. The dotnet-driven test skips by name without dotnet and fails by name under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1, as its neighbours do. Add no make target (make/cs.mk is not in PATHS): the test runs under go test ./internal/codegen/cstable/.

DONE-WHEN: TestCsDefaultReadIsStrict passes (no tests to run at BASE): a clamped, a kind-mismatched and a framing-damaged wire each make the plain Load, region Load and LoadBuilder refuse with Err() naming clamped, kind_mismatch and malformed, the Tolerant twins return the recovered value with the same counters Go's tolerant read reports for the same wire, ReadStrict answers the same reason, and a wire carrying only an unknown field reads clean; go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/cstable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/ ./test/conformance/... is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE.

