# C# carries the base64 text carrier: SaveText and LoadText, canonical, refusing by name

§16.8 says every table has both text carriers. The C# leg has the JSON one only: there is no <Name>SaveText or <Name>LoadText, so the canonical-base64 rule (dfac6b0ce) has nothing to apply to.

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.8 (both carriers; canonical base64: standard alphabet, padded, pad bits zero, no byte outside the alphabet and `=`, no whitespace; base64_not_canonical when dropping CR and LF leaves padded base64 that decodes but is not the canonical text, base64_damaged for every other failure; LoadText is the strict read). Oracle: TestGoLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 at d808c3f54. The JSON half (bytes fields inside JSON) is schema-go-json-base64-canonical, still WORKING on schema-go: out of scope here.

THE GAP (read at BASE, after the forward merge). `grep -c SaveText internal/codegen/cstable/*.go` is 0 at BASE.

THE TASK. In the NEW internal/codegen/cstable/textcarrier.go emit, for each root of both classes, <Name>SaveTextMeasure/<Name>SaveText (the Save wire as canonical padded standard base64, written without System.Convert's line breaks) and <Name>LoadText (decode strictly, then the strict read of cs-plain-load-is-strict-with-a-tolerant-twin; base64_damaged and base64_not_canonical are the reasons on Err()), and call the emitter from native.go's per-root surface. LoadText(SaveText(v)) equals the wire Save(v) byte for byte.

THE TESTS. The new test lives in the NEW file named above, in package cstable, and drives generated C# the way internal/codegen/cstable/messageform_held_test.go does (csDotnetToolchain: Roslyn csc plus dotnet exec, one build, one run): it generates the probe unit with the compiler, compiles it with a C# probe program, runs it and parses its lines. THE EXPECTED ANSWERS COME FROM SCHEMA-GO at d808c3f54: copy the oracle test's schema and its pinned bytes, reasons and values (the oracle is named under THE RULE), never a value worked out by hand; where the Go oracle prints wire bytes, the C# leg must print the same bytes. The dotnet-driven test skips by name without dotnet and fails by name under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1, as its neighbours do. Add no make target (make/cs.mk is not in PATHS): the test runs under go test ./internal/codegen/cstable/.

DONE-WHEN: TestCsLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 passes (no tests to run at BASE): Go's canonical texts load and round-trip byte for byte; a set pad bit, an inner `=`, a CR/LF and a missing pad each answer the reason Go's test pins (base64_not_canonical or base64_damaged); go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/cstable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/ is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE.

