The C# descriptor has ArrayBound and no UnboundedContainer column.

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §8.1 and §2.9 (UnboundedContainer true and ArrayBound 0 for a map, []T and an unbounded text list; false and the bound for [..N]T). Oracle: TestGoUnboundedDescriptorIsExplicit at d808c3f54 (the descriptor rows; the text-list and SaveText rows wait for their C# carry cards).

THE GAP (read at BASE, after the forward merge). `grep -c UnboundedContainer internal/codegen/cstable/*.go` is 0 at BASE.

THE TASK. Add the UnboundedContainer column to the C# TableFieldInfo (cstable.go) and fill it in view.go for every field; the 100000-entry round trip is done over the binary wire and JSON.

THE TESTS. The new test lives in the NEW file named above, in package cstable, and drives generated C# the way internal/codegen/cstable/messageform_held_test.go does (csDotnetToolchain: Roslyn csc plus dotnet exec, one build, one run): it generates the probe unit with the compiler, compiles it with a C# probe program, runs it and parses its lines. THE EXPECTED ANSWERS COME FROM SCHEMA-GO at d808c3f54: copy the oracle test's schema and its pinned bytes, reasons and values (the oracle is named under THE RULE), never a value worked out by hand; where the Go oracle prints wire bytes, the C# leg must print the same bytes. The dotnet-driven test skips by name without dotnet and fails by name under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1, as its neighbours do. Add no make target (make/cs.mk is not in PATHS): the test runs under go test ./internal/codegen/cstable/.

