# Elixir: one blob named from two slots is blob_shared

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family other rules, blob_shared: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.5 (A blob is OWNED BY ONE SLOT: every writer refuses to emit it; the tolerant read keeps the one node and counts each extra naming in the report's blob_shared counter; the strict read refuses it) and §16.7; oracle internal/codegen/gotable/blobnamedtwice_test.go (TestBlobNamedTwiceSeed24, TestBlobNamedTwiceWriters).

RED AT BASE (BASE is the base after elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f landed). `grep -c blob_shared internal/codegen/elixirtable/*.go` is 0; the report has no blob_shared counter (empty_report, variableform.go:1750-1760) and the JSON tally counts a node named twice as one label without refusing (tally_refs, variableform.go:2005-2008).

THE TASK. Add the blob_shared counter to the report; the tolerant load keeps the one node and counts each extra naming; the strict load and from_json refuse with `:blob_shared`; save, load_measure's writer twin and to_json refuse to emit a value whose two slots hold the same blob node (the node-numbering walk meets the second slot: one test there). Test TestElixirBlobNamedTwice in the new blobshared_test.go: the Go test's seed-24 wire (two slots naming one blob record) through both reads, and the writers' rows, with Go's verdicts and counts. Expected answers come from schema-go at d808c3f54 and are never typed from memory: bytes, texts and refusal reasons are read from the engine packages internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext and internal/tablepack inside the Go test (the way internal/codegen/elixirtable/textdifferential_test.go (read) uses them), and where the engine has no surface for the answer the expected value is the one the named Go test pins, cited by file and line in a comment. The Elixir probe is generated into t.TempDir() and run under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 (skip by name without the toolchain, fail by name with it), as keyed_test.go does; a Go test that only reads generator output is a unit test, one that runs elixir is a functional test reached from a make target in make/elixir.mk that fails on any SKIP and is listed in test-elixir.

DONE-WHEN: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable -run '^TestElixirBlobNamedTwice$' -v shows RUN and --- PASS, and the same command at BASE prints `testing: warning: no tests to run` (the test is new) while the gap named under RED AT BASE holds there; make test-elixir stays green; the committed generated Elixir is current (make test-elixir's generated-current and format checks green); make roadmap-check is clean.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Red first: write the test and run it at BASE: the strict load accepts the shared blob; keep the line.
STEP 3. Add the counter, the strict refusal and the writer refusals, regenerate.
Run the gate: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable/ ./compiler/, make test-elixir, ./build/conformance-harness run --only elixir, make roadmap-check and read the last line of each. When a test fails, name its file and say whether that file was changed by your work (yours) or is unchanged (already red at BASE: run the same test on the unchanged base to say so), and report that line first.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against the BASE: line's branch, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, what was deleted, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
STEP 6. End as JOB.md says: where JOB.md ends the card with its pull request, that is the end and there is nothing else to write, the gate's lines in the pull request body; where it asks for RESULT.md, write it in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report).

