# Elixir: carry `?map[K]V` — map presence

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family other rules and the maps feature: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.8 (an OPTIONAL MAP: a present empty map is not absent); oracle internal/codegen/gotable/mappresence_test.go TestGoMapPresence.

RED AT BASE (BASE is the base after elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f landed). compiler/tablesmaps.go refuseOptionalMaps, called from compiler/generate.go's Generate for every target but go, refuses `?map[K]V` for elixir (compiler/mappresence_refusal_test.go TestMapPresenceRefusedOffGo), and the Elixir map writer elides an empty map.

THE TASK. Carry the optional map: absent, present-empty and present-with-entries are three values on the wire and in JSON, at the engine's bytes and text; the plain map keeps eliding empty. Then register the carry: ONE line, `registerCarried(\"elixir\", <the optional-map construct constant>)`, in compiler/target_elixir.go's init(), using the registry schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries defines (compiler/carries.go (read), on this base through elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f); no edit to compiler/generate.go (read) or to the refusal's text. compiler/mappresence_refusal_test.go TestMapPresenceRefusedOffGo asks carries(lang, ...) and then expects elixir to generate with no edit of its own; it stays green for every other target. Test TestElixirMapPresence in the new mappresence_test.go: the Go test's rows, save byte-equal to the engine, load and from_json equal to its unpack. Expected answers come from schema-go at d808c3f54 and are never typed from memory: bytes, texts and refusal reasons are read from the engine packages internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext and internal/tablepack inside the Go test (the way internal/codegen/elixirtable/textdifferential_test.go (read) uses them), and where the engine has no surface for the answer the expected value is the one the named Go test pins, cited by file and line in a comment. The Elixir probe is generated into t.TempDir() and run under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 (skip by name without the toolchain, fail by name with it), as keyed_test.go does; a Go test that only reads generator output is a unit test, one that runs elixir is a functional test reached from a make target in make/elixir.mk that fails on any SKIP and is listed in test-elixir.

DONE-WHEN: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable -run '^TestElixirMapPresence$' -v shows RUN and --- PASS, and the same command at BASE prints `testing: warning: no tests to run` (the test is new) while the gap named under RED AT BASE holds there; go test ./compiler/ -run TestMapPresenceRefusedOffGo is green with elixir generating; the committed generated Elixir is current (make test-elixir's generated-current and format checks green); make roadmap-check is clean.

