# Elixir: carry `| required` — missing_required refuses the whole record at any depth, off-branch is not demanded, no default needed

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family required-off-branch: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.3 \"The | required marker\"; oracles TestGoRequiredInOffBranch (internal/codegen/gotable/requiredoffbranch_test.go, b4876bf60), TestGoRequiredExactFieldHasNoDefault (requirednodefault_test.go) and the whole-record-at-any-depth rule (136191a69).

RED AT BASE (BASE is the base after elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f landed). compiler/generate.go's Generate refuses `| required` for every target but go (\"target %q refuses | required — Go carries it first\", generate.go:104-105), held by compiler/required_test.go TestRequiredRefusedForEveryTargetButGo; variableform.go has no `required` anywhere (`grep -c required internal/codegen/elixirtable/variableform.go` is 0 outside comments).

THE TASK. Carry the marker in the variable form (a fixed table cannot declare it, §2.3): the descriptor carries `required: true` per field; the binary and JSON reads record a required field that is absent as missing_required naming the field, and the strict reads (load/2, from_json/2, from elixir-plain-load-is-the-strict-read) refuse the WHOLE root with `{:error, :missing_required, report}` whatever depth the missing field sits at, while the tolerant twins report it and keep the value; a required field inside a guard or union arm that is OFF is not demanded; a required field with no declared default needs none (§2.3); the writer always writes a required field. Then register the carry: ONE line, `registerCarried(\"elixir\", <the required construct constant>)`, in compiler/target_elixir.go's init(), using the registry schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries defines (compiler/carries.go (read), on this base through elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f); no edit to compiler/generate.go (read) or to the refusal's text. compiler/required_test.go TestRequiredRefusedForEveryTargetButGo asks carries(lang, ...) and then expects elixir to generate with no edit of its own; it stays green for every other target. Test TestElixirRequiredFieldRules in the new required_test.go: the probes of TestGoRequiredInOffBranch and TestGoRequiredExactFieldHasNoDefault in Elixir spelling, a required field missing at the root, one level down and inside a list element (each refusing the whole read), an off arm with its required field absent reading clean, all against the engine's strict read of the same bytes. Expected answers come from schema-go at d808c3f54 and are never typed from memory: bytes, texts and refusal reasons are read from the engine packages internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext and internal/tablepack inside the Go test (the way internal/codegen/elixirtable/textdifferential_test.go (read) uses them), and where the engine has no surface for the answer the expected value is the one the named Go test pins, cited by file and line in a comment. The Elixir probe is generated into t.TempDir() and run under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 (skip by name without the toolchain, fail by name with it), as keyed_test.go does; a Go test that only reads generator output is a unit test, one that runs elixir is a functional test reached from a make target in make/elixir.mk that fails on any SKIP and is listed in test-elixir.

DONE-WHEN: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable -run '^TestElixirRequiredFieldRules$' -v shows RUN and --- PASS, and the same command at BASE prints `testing: warning: no tests to run` (the test is new) while the gap named under RED AT BASE holds there; go test ./compiler/ -run TestRequiredRefusedForEveryTargetButGo is green with elixir generating; the committed generated Elixir is current (make test-elixir's generated-current and format checks green); make roadmap-check is clean.

