# Elixir generator fix: Comparisons and if/case on values the generator already knows (the constant-test group, 112 findings)

WHY. The Dialyzer gate (schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate) runs Dialyzer over the generated Elixir with no -Wno_* flags and compares the findings with make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected, one line per finding (`<file>:<line> <class>`). The roughly 487 findings it starts with are generator defects or dead code, split into one card per pattern group (coordinator decision, 2026-10-19). This card owns one group; the other groups are other elixir-dialyzer-* cards, so leave their lines in the file. Every group card regenerates the same generated trees and edits the same expected file, so the cards run one after another: this one DEPENDS-ON elixir-dialyzer-dead-error-branches.

THE FINDINGS. 62 x class exact_eq / guard_fail-family 'The test ... can never evaluate to true/false' (`pos_integer() == N` 26, `N /= N` 11, `N =:= N` 9, `N | N =:= N` 8, wider unions 8) and 50 x pattern_match 'The pattern false can never match the type true', the case-lowering of the same constant `if` (the two warnings often share one line). Files: TableMessage.ex (52, lines 612-822), Table.ex (31, including Table.ex:4360 in fixed-examples and table-tabledemo), WideText.ex (8), Tables.ex, FU1.ex, FU2.ex (4 each), Bench.ex (3, including Bench.ex:2748, triaged individually per the earlier route note), Caption.ex, Data.ex, RealWorld.ex (2 each); the `:1` lines are module-level. Emitters: internal/codegen/elixirtable/{messageform,variableform}.go and internal/codegen/elixir/{elixir,functions,wstring}.go (for example `if pad != 0` with a constant pad). Line numbers are from the r5 census and shift as the generator changes: the authority is the expected file at your BASE, the entries of the classes and messages named here.

THE FIX. Fold the comparison at generation time and emit only the branch that can run; never an @dialyzer nowarn attribute, never a flag. Fix it in the generator only, never by hand-editing generated output; regenerate every committed generated tree in PATHS with the repository's generate targets.

DONE-WHEN: every finding of this group is gone from a no-flags Dialyzer run on the corpus at the card's head and its lines are removed from make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected (other groups' lines stay, renumbered only where your change moved them, and the report shows the before/after count per class); the Dialyzer gate target exits 0 at the head; each changed emitter has a Go test RED at BASE (keep the failing line) and green at the head; no new finding appears; no -Wno_* flag, @dialyzer attribute or output filter is added anywhere; `git diff --stat <BASE>..HEAD` touches only PATHS; the report names other ports' generators that emit the same pattern (grep only, do not fix them).

STEP 1. Enter your worktree with cd <worktree path> && git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac, and never run the heavy tool on the studio.
STEP 2. Read the dialyzer gate's make file and make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected at BASE; run the gate once to confirm your group's lines reproduce. If they do not (another card already removed them), report that and stop with Verdict: HOLD.
