# Elixir generator fix: {:error, _} branches on calls that cannot return an error (29 findings, all in generated Table.ex)

WHY. The Dialyzer gate (schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate) runs Dialyzer over the generated Elixir with no -Wno_* flags and compares the findings with make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected, one line per finding (`<file>:<line> <class>`). The roughly 487 findings it starts with are generator defects or dead code, split into one card per pattern group (coordinator decision, 2026-10-19). This card owns one group; the other groups are other elixir-dialyzer-* cards, so leave their lines in the file. Every group card regenerates the same generated trees and edits the same expected file, so the cards run one after another: this one DEPENDS-ON elixir-dialyzer-union-arm-code-without-arms.

THE FINDINGS. Class pattern_match: `{:error, _}` can never match the type `{:ok, [any()], [any()]} | {:stop, [any()], [any()], non_neg_integer()}`. The walker that returns :ok | :stop is matched with an error arm (variableform.go emits `{:error, _} ->` at its lines 831, 3312 and 3535 at BASE). r5 lines include Table.ex:725, 741, 742, 764, 838 ... 6150 (26 distinct). Line numbers are from the r5 census and shift as the generator changes: the authority is the expected file at your BASE, the entries of the classes and messages named here.

THE FIX. Decide per call site: either the walker really can fail (then make it return the error and test that path, red at BASE) or the arm is dead (then drop it). Name which in the report; never an @dialyzer nowarn attribute, never a flag. Fix it in the generator only, never by hand-editing generated output; regenerate every committed generated tree in PATHS with the repository's generate targets.

DONE-WHEN: every finding of this group is gone from a no-flags Dialyzer run on the corpus at the card's head and its lines are removed from make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected (other groups' lines stay, renumbered only where your change moved them, and the report shows the before/after count per class); the Dialyzer gate target exits 0 at the head; each changed emitter has a Go test RED at BASE (keep the failing line) and green at the head; no new finding appears; no -Wno_* flag, @dialyzer attribute or output filter is added anywhere; `git diff --stat <BASE>..HEAD` touches only PATHS; the report names other ports' generators that emit the same pattern (grep only, do not fix them).

