# Elixir generator fix: Descriptor-dispatch clauses that can never match (the pattern group, 203 findings, all in generated Table.ex across the table-* and fixed-* units)

WHY. The Dialyzer gate (schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate) runs Dialyzer over the generated Elixir with no -Wno_* flags and compares the findings with make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected, one line per finding (`<file>:<line> <class>`). The roughly 487 findings it starts with are generator defects or dead code, split into one card per pattern group (coordinator decision, 2026-10-19). This card owns one group; the other groups are other elixir-dialyzer-* cards, so leave their lines in the file.

THE FINDINGS. Dialyzer classes pattern_match and pattern_match_cov on clauses that dispatch on a field descriptor map by its type tag: `#{t := :void}`, `#{t := :bool | :int | :float | :enum | :string | :wstring | :bytes | :list | :union | :table}` and the catch-all clause after them ('can never match the type' / 'can never match since previous clauses completely covered the type'). The generated runtime emits every descriptor arm for every schema, so in a unit whose layouts are all `t: :table` (or only `int | string | wstring`) Dialyzer proves the other arms dead. r5 census lines in Table.ex include 1001, 1003, 1008, 1011, 1014, 1020, 1065, 1258-1276 and Table.ex:1519 (fixed-fe2), which the earlier route note asked to be triaged individually. Line numbers are from the r5 census and shift as the generator changes: the authority is the expected file at your BASE, the entries of the classes and messages named here.

THE FIX. Emit only the descriptor arms the unit's layouts can reach (the generator knows the closed set of t: tags per unit), or restructure the dispatch so the arms are not specialised on a literal; never an @dialyzer nowarn attribute, never a flag. Fix it in the generator only, never by hand-editing generated output; regenerate every committed generated tree in PATHS with the repository's generate targets.

DONE-WHEN: every finding of this group is gone from a no-flags Dialyzer run on the corpus at the card's head and its lines are removed from make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected (other groups' lines stay, renumbered only where your change moved them, and the report shows the before/after count per class); the Dialyzer gate target exits 0 at the head; each changed emitter has a Go test RED at BASE (keep the failing line) and green at the head; no new finding appears; no -Wno_* flag, @dialyzer attribute or output filter is added anywhere; `git diff --stat <BASE>..HEAD` touches only PATHS; the report names other ports' generators that emit the same pattern (grep only, do not fix them).

STEP 1. Enter your worktree with cd <worktree path> && git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac, and never run the heavy tool on the studio.
STEP 2. Read the dialyzer gate's make file and make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected at BASE; run the gate once to confirm your group's lines reproduce. If they do not (another card already removed them), report that and stop with Verdict: HOLD.
STEP 3. Fix the emitter(s), add the RED-at-BASE Go tests, regenerate, rerun the gate, update make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected.
STEP 6. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against sprint/schema-elixir, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
