# Elixir generator fix: Guards that can never succeed (the guard group, 15 findings)

WHY. The Dialyzer gate (schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate) runs Dialyzer over the generated Elixir with no -Wno_* flags and compares the findings with make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected, one line per finding (`<file>:<line> <class>`). The roughly 487 findings it starts with are generator defects or dead code, split into one card per pattern group (coordinator decision, 2026-10-19). This card owns one group; the other groups are other elixir-dialyzer-* cards, so leave their lines in the file. Every group card regenerates the same generated trees and edits the same expected file, so the cards run one after another: this one DEPENDS-ON elixir-dialyzer-constant-tests.

THE FINDINGS. Class guard_fail: in the fixed-form runtimes `_x :: 1 | 2 | 3 >= 8 can never succeed` (KeyedFixed.ex:427, MessagesFixed.ex:1290, PackFixed.ex:450, ScalarsFixed.ex:427 and 501, TablesFixed.ex:508, V1Fixed.ex:692 and 728, V2Fixed.ex:798 and 834, emitted by fixedelixir.go / fixedruntime.go: a width or count guard checked against a bound its type can never reach), and in Table.ex:1814 and 1817 `_ :: :list | :union =:= :blob can never succeed`. Line numbers are from the r5 census and shift as the generator changes: the authority is the expected file at your BASE, the entries of the classes and messages named here.

THE FIX. Emit the guard only where the bound is reachable, or derive the bound from the value's real range; if a guard is a needed safety check on hostile input, show the input that reaches it in a test. Never an @dialyzer nowarn attribute, never a flag. Fix it in the generator only, never by hand-editing generated output; regenerate every committed generated tree in PATHS with the repository's generate targets.

