# Elixir generator fix: Union-arm code emitted for units with no union arms (the call and unused-function group, 128 findings, all in generated Table.ex)

WHY. The Dialyzer gate (schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate) runs Dialyzer over the generated Elixir with no -Wno_* flags and compares the findings with make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected, one line per finding (`<file>:<line> <class>`). The roughly 487 findings it starts with are generator defects or dead code, split into one card per pattern group (coordinator decision, 2026-10-19). This card owns one group; the other groups are other elixir-dialyzer-* cards, so leave their lines in the file. Every group card regenerates the same generated trees and edits the same expected file, so the cards run one after another: this one DEPENDS-ON elixir-dialyzer-descriptor-dispatch-clauses.

THE FINDINGS. 96 x class call: `maps:get(_union@1, #{})` will never return, the arm lookup into an empty arms map (r5 lines include Table.ex:234, 250, 251, 273, 375 ... 8217, 83 distinct lines); 32 x class unused_fun: `arm_content/5` (16) and `read_arm_payload/7` (16) will never be called. All come from the union-arm helpers being emitted where the unit has no union. Line numbers are from the r5 census and shift as the generator changes: the authority is the expected file at your BASE, the entries of the classes and messages named here.

THE FIX. Emit the union-arm lookup and the arm_content / read_arm_payload helpers only for units that have union arms (or emit a reachable no-arms form); never an @dialyzer nowarn attribute, never a flag. Fix it in the generator only, never by hand-editing generated output; regenerate every committed generated tree in PATHS with the repository's generate targets.

DONE-WHEN: every finding of this group is gone from a no-flags Dialyzer run on the corpus at the card's head and its lines are removed from make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected (other groups' lines stay, renumbered only where your change moved them, and the report shows the before/after count per class); the Dialyzer gate target exits 0 at the head; each changed emitter has a Go test RED at BASE (keep the failing line) and green at the head; no new finding appears; no -Wno_* flag, @dialyzer attribute or output filter is added anywhere; `git diff --stat <BASE>..HEAD` touches only PATHS; the report names other ports' generators that emit the same pattern (grep only, do not fix them).

STEP 1. Enter your worktree with cd <worktree path> && git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac, and never run the heavy tool on the studio.
STEP 2. Read the dialyzer gate's make file and make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected at BASE; run the gate once to confirm your group's lines reproduce. If they do not (another card already removed them), report that and stop with Verdict: HOLD.
STEP 3. Fix the emitter(s), add the RED-at-BASE Go tests, regenerate, rerun the gate, update make/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate.expected.
STEP 6. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against sprint/schema-elixir, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
STEP 7. End as JOB.md says (docs/SPEC-CARD-CONTRACT.md): where JOB.md ends the card with its pull request, that is the end and there is nothing else to write, the gate's lines in the pull request body; where it asks for RESULT.md, write it in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report). The report starts with Verdict: LAND or Verdict: HOLD on line 1 and Head: <sha> on line 2.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.
No gh, no push: JOB.md's finish does both, from outside the wall. Never merge. Every `go test` gets `-timeout 600s`; every new test opens with `t.Parallel()`.
Unit tests use no real time, no sockets, no network and no outside services: time is an argument and a test clock starts at 1000.0. Fuzzing, analyzers that run for minutes and anything needing the network are functional tier, behind the slow gate (read internal/slowtest), never in a unit test.
Install tools only from official sources and only through the fleet play; never print or store a secret or token.
Make the smallest change that does the task, with no refactor beyond what the task names.
Never read outside the job's working directory; never search /, ~ or /Volumes; search inside the checkout only.
ROADMAP.md and docs/roadmap.sexp are lander-owned ledgers inside every card's PATHS: commit the ROADMAP.md the roadmap tool renders if the card's work moves an item.
A test that SKIPS is not a pass: a gate line must show --- PASS. A red is pre-existing only if reproduced at BASE in the same environment.
Finish LAND with --head <sha>; finish HOLD with --failed. \"Not done\" is a welcome report; a green claim you did not run is not.")
