# Elixir: the variable and fixed file wires carry the integrity trailer

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family integrity, the file wires: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.14 (the `integrity` table-line key and the CRC-32C trailer) and §3.4; oracles TestGoWireIntegrityCheck (internal/codegen/gotable/integrity_test.go) and TestGoWireIntegrityFixedForm (integrityfixed_test.go).

RED AT BASE (BASE is the base after elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f landed). compiler/generate.go's Generate refuses integrity for every target but go (compiler/integrity_refusal_test.go TestIntegrityRefusedOffGo) and `grep -c integrity internal/codegen/elixirtable/*.go` is 0.

THE TASK. For a table that declares integrity, the variable `save` and the fixed `<t>_fixed_save` append the trailer exactly as internal/tablewire does (the algorithm, the width, the placement), and both loads check it before decoding: a missing trailer and a mismatched one each refuse by the name §2.14 gives, through the strict and tolerant loads alike; a table that does not declare it is byte-identical to today. The central refusal stays until elixir-message-form-carries-integrity lands the message form and lifts it: this card's test calls the elixirtable generator directly, never compiler.Generate. Test TestElixirWireIntegrityCheck in the new integrity_test.go: a variable and a fixed root declaring integrity; saved bytes equal the engine's; a flipped body byte, a flipped trailer byte and a cut trailer each refuse with Go's reason; an undeclared table's bytes are unchanged. Expected answers come from schema-go at d808c3f54 and are never typed from memory: bytes, texts and refusal reasons are read from the engine packages internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext and internal/tablepack inside the Go test (the way internal/codegen/elixirtable/textdifferential_test.go (read) uses them), and where the engine has no surface for the answer the expected value is the one the named Go test pins, cited by file and line in a comment. The Elixir probe is generated into t.TempDir() and run under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 (skip by name without the toolchain, fail by name with it), as keyed_test.go does; a Go test that only reads generator output is a unit test, one that runs elixir is a functional test reached from a make target in make/elixir.mk that fails on any SKIP and is listed in test-elixir.

DONE-WHEN: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable -run '^TestElixirWireIntegrityCheck$' -v shows RUN and --- PASS, and the same command at BASE prints `testing: warning: no tests to run` (the test is new) while the gap named under RED AT BASE holds there; make test-elixir stays green; the committed generated Elixir is current (make test-elixir's generated-current and format checks green); make roadmap-check is clean.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Red first: write the test and run it at BASE: no trailer is written; keep the line.
STEP 3. Write the CRC-32C, the trailer and the checks in both forms, regenerate.
Run the gate: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable/ ./compiler/, make test-elixir, ./build/conformance-harness run --only elixir, make roadmap-check and read the last line of each. When a test fails, name its file and say whether that file was changed by your work (yours) or is unchanged (already red at BASE: run the same test on the unchanged base to say so), and report that line first.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against the BASE: line's branch, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, what was deleted, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
