# Elixir: the fixed-form load and the message-form read are strict by default

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family strict-read, the fixed class: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5 and §11; oracle TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict's \"fixed\" subtest (internal/codegen/gotable/strictdefault_test.go: Load, FromJson, LoadText, FixedLoad, LoadMessages over a clean, a clamped, a kind-mismatched and a truncated wire).

