# Elixir: from_json_with and to_json_with take the three JSON options

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Feature: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.2 (THREE OPTIONS MEET A TEXT ANOTHER LIBRARY WROTE: null as empty on read, omit defaults and compact on write; \"Every other target owes them\"), including the family-11 rule that omit-defaults always writes a `required` field (hence the need on elixir-carries-required). Oracle the Go leg's <T>FromJsonWith / <T>ToJsonWith and its tests.

RED AT BASE (BASE is the base after elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f landed). variableform.go has no options argument on from_json or to_json (`grep -c 'from_json_with\\|to_json_with\\|omit' internal/codegen/elixirtable/variableform.go` is 0).

THE TASK. Add `from_json_with(table, text, opts)` (strict, as from_json is), `from_json_tolerant_with`, and `to_json_with(table, value, opts)` taking a keyword list or map `null_as_empty`, `omit_defaults`, `compact`, with §16.2's rules exactly: null as empty empties an array-shaped or map field uncounted; omit defaults writes no key for a value at its default, decided on storage conservatively, always writes a required field, never elides an array element, writes every field of a &node definition that would elide all; compact removes whitespace outside strings with no trailing newline; all three off is today's text byte for byte. Test TestElixirJsonOptions in the new jsonoptions_test.go: each option alone and together over the conformance corpus roots Elixir carries, texts byte-equal to Go's With calls, reads landing the same instance. Expected answers come from schema-go at d808c3f54 and are never typed from memory: bytes, texts and refusal reasons are read from the engine packages internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext and internal/tablepack inside the Go test (the way internal/codegen/elixirtable/textdifferential_test.go (read) uses them), and where the engine has no surface for the answer the expected value is the one the named Go test pins, cited by file and line in a comment. The Elixir probe is generated into t.TempDir() and run under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 (skip by name without the toolchain, fail by name with it), as keyed_test.go does; a Go test that only reads generator output is a unit test, one that runs elixir is a functional test reached from a make target in make/elixir.mk that fails on any SKIP and is listed in test-elixir.

