SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Feature: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.9.3 (a rewrite is the source; a leaf edit replaces one token span), second half of §16.9. Oracle internal/codegen/gotable/textform.go's writer and edit, and its tests.

RED AT BASE (BASE is the base after elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f landed). after elixir-textform-reads-the-hand-editable-form the Elixir textform reads only: there is no writer and no leaf edit.

THE TASK. Emit, from a new internal/codegen/elixirtable/textformedit.go, the document writer and the leaf edit with Go's semantics: writing a value produces Go's document text byte for byte; an edit of one leaf replaces exactly that token span and leaves every other byte (comments, spacing) as it was; an edit that would change the value's shape refuses by Go's name. Test TestElixirTextFormEditsLeaves in the new textformedit_test.go: Go's writer and edit cases, output bytes equal to Go's. Expected answers come from schema-go at d808c3f54 and are never typed from memory: bytes, texts and refusal reasons are read from the engine packages internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext and internal/tablepack inside the Go test (the way internal/codegen/elixirtable/textdifferential_test.go (read) uses them), and where the engine has no surface for the answer the expected value is the one the named Go test pins, cited by file and line in a comment. The Elixir probe is generated into t.TempDir() and run under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 (skip by name without the toolchain, fail by name with it), as keyed_test.go does; a Go test that only reads generator output is a unit test, one that runs elixir is a functional test reached from a make target in make/elixir.mk that fails on any SKIP and is listed in test-elixir.

