# Elixir: timestamp text is strict RFC 3339 section 5.6 date-time, and the elixir target carries timestamp

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family rfc3339, second half: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.11 and §16.2 (7fb89e941): the JSON text of a timestamp is strict RFC 3339 §5.6 date-time, and a text that is not is refused by name, timestamp_not_rfc3339. Oracles internal/rfc3339 TestStrictRFC3339 (its case table), TestGoTimestampStrictRFC3339 and TestTextFormTimestampStrictRFC3339.

RED AT BASE (BASE is the base after elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f landed). after elixir-carries-timestamp-on-the-wire the JSON reader and writer still have no timestamp row (`grep -c timestamp internal/codegen/elixirtable/variableform.go` counts only that card's wire lines), and compiler/generate.go's Generate still refuses the kind for elixir.

THE TASK. Write the timestamp's JSON text as the engine writes it (internal/tabletext's write.go spelling: the canonical RFC 3339 text, its fraction digits and its zone) and read it with a strict RFC 3339 §5.6 parser that refuses, by `:timestamp_not_rfc3339` on the report naming the field, every spelling internal/rfc3339's TestStrictRFC3339 refuses (lowercase t or z, a space separator, a missing zone, a leap second where §2.11 says, out-of-range fields, an instant outside the domain), accepting every one it accepts; the strict from_json refuses, the tolerant twin reports it malformed as Go's does. Then register the carry: ONE line, `registerCarried(\"elixir\", <the timestamp construct constant>)`, in compiler/target_elixir.go's init(), using the registry schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries defines (compiler/carries.go (read), on this base through elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f); no edit to compiler/generate.go (read) or to the refusal's text. the compiler tests that hold the timestamp refusal asks carries(lang, ...) and then expects elixir to generate with no edit of its own; it stays green for every other target. Test TestElixirTimestampStrictRFC3339 in the new timestamptext_test.go: every row of internal/rfc3339's case table through from_json (accept or refuse equal to the Go parser's verdict, read in the test by calling the internal/rfc3339 package), and to_json of the five wire-card values byte-equal to the engine's text. Expected answers come from schema-go at d808c3f54 and are never typed from memory: bytes, texts and refusal reasons are read from the engine packages internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext and internal/tablepack inside the Go test (the way internal/codegen/elixirtable/textdifferential_test.go (read) uses them), and where the engine has no surface for the answer the expected value is the one the named Go test pins, cited by file and line in a comment. The Elixir probe is generated into t.TempDir() and run under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 (skip by name without the toolchain, fail by name with it), as keyed_test.go does; a Go test that only reads generator output is a unit test, one that runs elixir is a functional test reached from a make target in make/elixir.mk that fails on any SKIP and is listed in test-elixir.

DONE-WHEN: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable -run '^TestElixirTimestampStrictRFC3339$' -v shows RUN and --- PASS, and the same command at BASE prints `testing: warning: no tests to run` (the test is new) while the gap named under RED AT BASE holds there; elixir generates a unit with a timestamp field through compiler.Generate; the committed generated Elixir is current (make test-elixir's generated-current and format checks green); make roadmap-check is clean.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Red first: write the test and run it at BASE: from_json has no timestamp row; keep the line.
STEP 3. Write the text writer and the strict parser, register the construct, regenerate.
Run the gate: SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/elixirtable/ ./compiler/, make test-elixir, ./build/conformance-harness run --only elixir, make roadmap-check and read the last line of each. When a test fails, name its file and say whether that file was changed by your work (yours) or is unchanged (already red at BASE: run the same test on the unchanged base to say so), and report that line first.
