# Java carries `integrity`: the CRC-32C trailer on the variable wire, missing or mismatched refused by name

SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18): \"We do all features across all languages.\" Full parity of the Java port with schema-go at d808c3f54 (the oracle, which reaches this base through java-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md at that commit.

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.14: a table line `integrity` puts a CRC-32C trailer on the wire; a missing or mismatched trailer is refused by name (integrity_mismatch).

THE GAP AT BASE. At BASE (after the forward merge) compiler/generate.go refuses integrity for java (TestIntegrityRefusedOffGo); `grep -c -i 'integrity\\|crc' internal/codegen/javatable/*.go` is 0.

THE TASK. Carry the trailer in the Java variable save, measure, load and retain paths (java.util.zip.CRC32C), refusing missing and mismatched trailers by name, matching Go's bytes. The fixed and message forms are the next card: until it lands, the Java emitter refuses a fixed table that declares integrity by name (in javatable.go's own refusal), naming that card. Register Java as carrying this construct's key in compiler/carries_java.go, the per-target file schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries creates (it arrives at this base with the forward merge holding Java's empty registerCarries call; it is on NEW only because the lint reads the pre-merge base): add the key(s) named below to that call and nowhere else. compiler/generate.go (read), compiler/carries.go (read) and the refusal tests are not edited; the registry then holds every other target to the refusal while Java generates the construct, which TestEachTargetDeclaresWhatItCarries and the construct's refusal test show. Key: integrity.

TESTS. A Go test that only reads the generator's output is a unit test: it uses no real time, sockets, network or outside services. A test that compiles or runs Java (javac, java) is a functional test: it finds the JDK through javaTools (internal/codegen/javatable/fixedform_test.go), skips by name when there is none and SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS is unset, fails by name when SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1. Expected answers come from schema-go: generate the same probe schema for Go in the same test (the gotable runGenerated pattern, or the engine packages internal/tablewire and internal/tabletext) and compare bytes, reports and reason names; never type an expected byte by hand. Every new test opens with t.Parallel().

