SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18): \"We do all features across all languages.\" Full parity of the Java port with schema-go at d808c3f54 (the oracle, which reaches this base through java-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md at that commit.

THE RULE. docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.3 (every refusal of the fixed load has a name, framing damage included) and docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.4: a count past the PLAN's bound refuses `count_over_bound`, a length past the plan's cap refuses `length_over_bound`, both before any destination byte is written (4edb98c8a); the text content rules refuse `text_ill_formed`.

THE GAP AT BASE. At BASE Java's Reason enum (fixedruntime.go near line 460) has no truncated, reservedNotZero, countOverBound, lengthOverBound or layoutUnknown member; `grep -c 'over_bound\\|OverBound' internal/codegen/javatable/fixedruntime.go` is 0; opCount (near line 69) still clamps a count to the bound and counts clamped, and the four framing-damage returns set malformed with Reason.none.

THE TASK. Bring Java's fixed Reason enum to Go's TableFixedReason set at d808c3f54 (same names, the Java member's spelling() answering Go's string), name every -1 of the emitted fixed load (the framing-damage returns keep report.malformed beside the name), and make opCount and opText refuse count_over_bound / length_over_bound before writing any destination byte where the plan's bound is exceeded, exactly where Go's runtime refuses. Update the fixed versioning tests that pinned the old clamp (fixedversioning_count_clamp_ends_test.go and the t04-t07 roadmap tests) to Go's new answers, citing 4edb98c8a.

TESTS. A Go test that only reads the generator's output is a unit test: it uses no real time, sockets, network or outside services. A test that compiles or runs Java (javac, java) is a functional test: it finds the JDK through javaTools (internal/codegen/javatable/fixedform_test.go), skips by name when there is none and SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS is unset, fails by name when SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1. Expected answers come from schema-go: generate the same probe schema for Go in the same test (the gotable runGenerated pattern, or the engine packages internal/tablewire and internal/tabletext) and compare bytes, reports and reason names; never type an expected byte by hand. Every new test opens with t.Parallel().

