DONE-WHEN: (1) `SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s -v ./internal/codegen/javatable/ -run '^TestJavaDefaultReadIsStrict$'` prints RUN and PASS and no SKIP at the head, and the same command at the unchanged BASE prints `no tests to run` (the test is new) while the BASE-side probe the test holds fails (paste both lines); (2) the test mirrors TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict's variable subtests over the same schema: a clean wire, a clamped wire, a kind-mismatched wire and a truncated wire through load and fromJson, and asserts null plus the same reason name Go's Err() gives, while loadTolerant/fromJsonTolerant return the value Go's LoadTolerant/FromJsonTolerant return with the same counters; (3) `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/javatable/ ./compiler/` is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE (with the BASE run); `make test-java JAVA=\"$JAVA\" JAVAC=\"$JAVAC\"` has no red target the BASE run does not also have (each named); make roadmap-check is clean.

