# sprint/schema-js takes sprint/schema-go: the JavaScript base forward-merge

THE TASK. sprint/schema-js is about 686 commits behind sprint/schema-go (64dc1ddd when carded; GO TIP below is the tip you fetch, at or after it). Merge origin/sprint/schema-go into the base as ONE merge commit on the card branch: git fetch origin, then git merge --no-ff GO TIP. Never a rebase, never a squash, never a force-push. A trial merge on 2026-10-18 left these conflicts (a newer GO TIP may add a few; resolve those by the same rules): ROADMAP.md, docs/roadmap.sexp, internal/codegen/jstable/fixedruntime.go. Resolve each conflict keeping BOTH sides' intent, by these rules and no others: shared Go and IR code (ir/, internal/check/, internal/parser/, compiler/, internal/codegen/gotable/, tools/, .github/) takes GO TIP's version; port-specific code keeps the port's version, adapted to the new IR; spec text (docs/*.md) merges both rewrites, each statement true of the merged code; ROADMAP.md is regenerated with make roadmap, never hand-edited; the roadmap sexp ledgers (docs/roadmap.sexp, docs/roadmap-evidence/*.sexp) keep each row's true state at the merge head. jstable/fixedruntime.go is port-specific: keep the JS base's behaviour, adapted to the IR GO TIP carries; the JS fixed-form tests in internal/codegen/jstable are the judge. Then regenerate the goldens, the generated trees and the bench the merge leaves stale with the repository's own Makefile targets, and commit the regenerated files in the merge commit or a second commit on the same branch. Nothing else changes: no rule is ported here.

