# JavaScript carries bounded text lists: `[N]string(M)`, `[E]string(M)`, `[..N]string(M)` and `[..N]?string(M)`

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.13 \"Text lists: `rules [..16]string(64)`\": a list of text is COUNTED; its wire, its storage, its fixed-form layout where the class allows, and its JSON spelling, as §2.13 states and Go's generated code does. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/stringarrays_test.go TestGoTableStringArraysAndJSONArrayRoot (the text-list half; the array root is js-carries-the-json-array-root).

THE GAP AT BASE (merged view). compiler/generate.go's refuseTextForms (compiler/tablesstringarrays.go at d808c3f54) refuses every text list for js (TestStringArraysRefusedOffGo), and internal/codegen/jstable/fixedform.go variableFieldRefusalNamed refuses \"an array of strings or byte strings\" by name besides.

REGISTER, DO NOT EDIT THE CENTRAL REFUSAL. schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries (a true need of this card) moved every \"Go carries it first\" decision into one list per target: compiler/carries.go's closed key set, and compiler/carries_js.go holding ONE init() with `registerCarries(\"js\", ...)`. Carry the construct in the JS emitter, then add the key `text-list` to that one call in compiler/carries_js.go; that one line is the whole compiler change (compiler/generate.go, refuseTextForms and refuseOptionalMaps are not edited, and the TestXRefusedOffGo tests already ask carries(lang, key), so they now expect js to generate while every other non-Go target still refuses by name). compiler/carries_js.go is on this card's NEW: line because it arrives with the forward merge, not at BASE's tip; it is the only compiler/ file this card edits. refuseTextForms answers four keys (text-list, unbounded-text, array-root, text-list-total): this card registers text-list only, so the unbounded spellings and the array root still refuse js by name.

THE TASK. Carry the four bounded spellings in the JS storage class, the variable wire (write, read, clamp, the content rules: UTF-8 validity and no zero byte, §2.13, §4.2), the fixed form where §3.4 allows a text list, and the JSON text (§16.2); drop \"an array of strings\" from variableFieldRefusalNamed for these spellings.

THE TESTS. TestJsTableBoundedTextLists (new): the oracle's bounded-list schemas and values, wire and JSON bytes equal Go's, reads equal Go's (past-bound counts and lengths clamp and count as Go's do), a zero byte in an element is malformed as Go's read says. Red at BASE.

