# JavaScript carries `integrity = \"crc32c\"` on the variable-form file: the CRC-32C trailer written and checked

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.14 \"The integrity check: `integrity`\" and §3: a table declaring `integrity = \"crc32c\"` saves its variable-form file with a CRC-32C trailer, every read checks it before decoding any field, a missing or mismatched trailer refuses by name, and a table without the key writes exactly the bytes it wrote before. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/integrity_test.go TestGoWireIntegrityCheck (no single-bit flip of any byte decodes as a value).

THE GAP AT BASE (merged view). compiler/generate.go refuses the key for js (`target \"js\" refuses the construct integrity on table ...`, compiler/integrity_refusal_test.go TestIntegrityRefusedOffGo).

REGISTER, DO NOT EDIT THE CENTRAL REFUSAL. schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries (a true need of this card) moved every \"Go carries it first\" decision into one list per target: compiler/carries.go's closed key set, and compiler/carries_js.go holding ONE init() with `registerCarries(\"js\", ...)`. Carry the construct in the JS emitter, then add the key `integrity` to that one call in compiler/carries_js.go; that one line is the whole compiler change (compiler/generate.go, refuseTextForms and refuseOptionalMaps are not edited, and the TestXRefusedOffGo tests already ask carries(lang, key), so they now expect js to generate while every other non-Go target still refuses by name). compiler/carries_js.go is on this card's NEW: line because it arrives with the forward merge, not at BASE's tip; it is the only compiler/ file this card edits. This card carries the VARIABLE class; until js-carries-integrity-on-the-fixed-and-message-forms lands, the JS leg refuses `integrity` on a FIXED table by name inside jstable (§11), so TestIntegrityRefusedOffGo's fixed half must be told js still refuses it there: put that one test edit here.

THE TASK. A CRC-32C (Castagnoli, reflected 0x82F63B78, table built once at module load) in new internal/codegen/jstable/integrity.go's emitted runtime; Save/Measure/SaveText write the trailer; Load, LoadTolerant, ReadStrict and LoadText check it first and refuse by Go's names; LoadMeasure accounts for it as Go's does.

THE TESTS. TestJsWireIntegrityCheck (new) uses the oracle's Ledger and Plain tables: Ledger's saved bytes equal Go's byte for byte, Plain's equal its pre-key bytes, every single-bit flip of every byte of Ledger's file refuses with the name Go's read gives, and a stripped trailer refuses as Go's does. Red at BASE.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

DONE-WHEN: (1) TestJsWireIntegrityCheck passes and fails at BASE; (2) `grep -c '\"integrity\"' compiler/carries_js.go` is 0 at BASE (after the merge) and 1 at the head; TestIntegrityRefusedOffGo passes with js generating the variable table and still refusing the fixed one; (3) the STEP 4 gate green or reds named as present at BASE.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Red first: write the new test, run it at BASE (this card's base, with js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f merged) and keep the failing line.
STEP 3. Find the cause, then fix it in the files PATHS names, and only those. Cite the SPEC-TABLES section from each emitter function that implements the rule. Regenerate the committed generated/ outputs with the repository's own make targets (make/js.mk) so generated/ is byte-identical to a fresh generation.
