# JavaScript carries `?T` whose T holds a pointer: every edge walk gates on presence

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.3: for `?T` over a variable closure every walk that follows pointer edges visits T's edges only when the presence companion is set, and an absent value owns no node; absent, present-with-text and present-empty round-trip the wire, base64 and JSON; a present value then cleared and saved writes no stale node through save, measure, the retaining save, the cook and the JSON writer. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/optionalvariable_test.go TestGoOptionalVariableClosureTable.

THE GAP AT BASE (merged view). compiler/generate.go refuses `optional over a variable closure on field ...` for js (compiler/optionalvariable_refusal_test.go TestOptionalVariableRefusedOffGo).

REGISTER, DO NOT EDIT THE CENTRAL REFUSAL. schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries (a true need of this card) moved every \"Go carries it first\" decision into one list per target: compiler/carries.go's closed key set, and compiler/carries_js.go holding ONE init() with `registerCarries(\"js\", ...)`. Carry the construct in the JS emitter, then add the key `optional-variable-closure` to that one call in compiler/carries_js.go; that one line is the whole compiler change (compiler/generate.go, refuseTextForms and refuseOptionalMaps are not edited, and the TestXRefusedOffGo tests already ask carries(lang, key), so they now expect js to generate while every other non-Go target still refuses by name). compiler/carries_js.go is on this card's NEW: line because it arrives with the forward merge, not at BASE's tip; it is the only compiler/ file this card edits.

THE TASK. Gate TableVariableEdges / TableVariableFieldEdges / TableVariableNumber, the retaining save (retain.go), the cook writer (cookwrite.go) and the JSON writer's graph walk on presence; the absent value's measure equals the measure without the pointer.

THE TESTS. TestJsOptionalVariableClosureTable (new): the oracle's Inner/Outer schemas and the cleared-value case, wire bytes, measures and JSON text equal Go's. Red at BASE.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

