# JavaScript's JSON text form honours `| required`: always written, a missing one refuses FromJson

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5 (\"The text read counts a missing required field as the binary read does\") and §16.2 (omit-defaults writes a required field): a JSON object that leaves a `| required` field out counts missing_required once, naming the fields, so the plain FromJson refuses it and FromJsonTolerant answers false with the count; a required field off its branch is not demanded; ToJson under omit-defaults writes every required field. Oracle: the JSON legs of TestGoRequiredInOffBranch and TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict.

THE GAP. After js-carries-required-on-the-wire the binary wire honours the marker but the JS text reader (TableVariableReadKeys) does not demand it and the writer may elide it at its zero value.

THE TASK. Demand required fields in the text read (after guards are known), name them in the reason, refuse on FromJson and answer false on FromJsonTolerant with the count; never omit a required field in ToJson.

