# JavaScript carries `| required` on the variable and message wires: written always, demanded on read, off-branch not demanded

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.3 \"The `| required` marker\": a required field always rides (omit-defaults never elides it, §16.2), has no declared default, and a read that does not find it counts `missing_required` once, naming the field, at any depth, refusing the WHOLE record (136191a69); the strict read refuses it with missing_required. A required field inside a guard/union arm that is OFF is absent from the wire and not demanded; with the branch on it must ride. Oracles: internal/codegen/gotable/requiredoffbranch_test.go TestGoRequiredInOffBranch, internal/codegen/gotable/requirednodefault_test.go TestGoRequiredExactFieldHasNoDefault, and the missing_required cases of TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict.

THE GAP AT BASE (in the merged view). compiler/generate.go refuses `| required` for js (`target \"js\" refuses | required — Go carries it first`), so no JS unit can declare it.

REGISTER, DO NOT EDIT THE CENTRAL REFUSAL. schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries (a true need of this card) moved every \"Go carries it first\" decision into one list per target: compiler/carries.go's closed key set, and compiler/carries_js.go holding ONE init() with `registerCarries(\"js\", ...)`. Carry the construct in the JS emitter, then add the key `required` to that one call in compiler/carries_js.go; that one line is the whole compiler change (compiler/generate.go, refuseTextForms and refuseOptionalMaps are not edited, and the TestXRefusedOffGo tests already ask carries(lang, key), so they now expect js to generate while every other non-Go target still refuses by name). compiler/carries_js.go is on this card's NEW: line because it arrives with the forward merge, not at BASE's tip; it is the only compiler/ file this card edits.

THE TASK. In the JS variable writer, write a required field whatever its value (no elision); in the variable reader, count missing_required naming the field when a required field is absent, refuse the whole record, and evaluate guards/arms first so an off branch demands nothing; the strict Load refuses with missing_required. The message form follows the same rule if its emitter writes the field set (messagebatch.go is outside PATHS: if the message form needs a change, say so in the report as PATHS-PROPOSED rather than editing it). The JSON half is js-carries-required-in-the-text-form.

THE TESTS. TestJsRequiredOnTheWire (new) runs the oracles' schemas (Current/Legacy with `if active { req int32 | required }`, the exact-field no-default case, a required field two tables deep): wire bytes of each value equal Go's, a Legacy wire read by Current with the branch off reads clean and with it on refuses missing_required as Go's strict read does, and the tolerant read's counters equal Go's. Red at BASE (generation refused).

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

DONE-WHEN: (1) TestJsRequiredOnTheWire passes and fails at BASE (the refusal line is the red); (2) `grep -c '\"required\"' compiler/carries_js.go` is 0 at BASE (after the merge) and 1 at the head; the compiler/ refusal test passes with js generating and every other non-Go target still refusing; (3) the STEP 4 gate green or reds named as present at BASE.

