# JavaScript carries a text list's `| total = N` byte bound on every writer and reader

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.13 (the TOTAL): `| total = N` bounds the sum of a text list's element bytes; writers refuse a value past it (Save and Measure -1, ToJsonMeasure -1, the retaining save -1); readers keep the longest prefix within the total, drop the rest, count clamped once naming the field, and the strict read refuses clamped. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/listtotalbytes_test.go TestGoTextListTotalBytesBound (all four spellings).

THE GAP. The JS leg refuses `text list total on field ...` (compiler/listtotalbytes_refusal_test.go TestListTotalBytesRefusedOffGo).

REGISTER, DO NOT EDIT THE CENTRAL REFUSAL. schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries (a true need of this card) moved every \"Go carries it first\" decision into one list per target: compiler/carries.go's closed key set, and compiler/carries_js.go holding ONE init() with `registerCarries(\"js\", ...)`. Carry the construct in the JS emitter, then add the key `text-list-total` to that one call in compiler/carries_js.go; that one line is the whole compiler change (compiler/generate.go, refuseTextForms and refuseOptionalMaps are not edited, and the TestXRefusedOffGo tests already ask carries(lang, key), so they now expect js to generate while every other non-Go target still refuses by name). compiler/carries_js.go is on this card's NEW: line because it arrives with the forward merge, not at BASE's tip; it is the only compiler/ file this card edits.

THE TASK. Carry the total on the variable writer and reader, the JSON writer and reader and the retaining save, on [..N]string(M), [..N]?string(M), []string(M), []?string(M), nested tables included.

THE TESTS. TestJsTextListTotalBytesBound (new): the oracle's Wide/narrow pair and values, writer refusals, reader prefixes, counters and reasons equal Go's. Red at BASE.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

DONE-WHEN: (1) TestJsTextListTotalBytesBound passes and fails at BASE; (2) `grep -c '\"text-list-total\"' compiler/carries_js.go` is 0 at BASE (after the merge) and 1 at the head; TestListTotalBytesRefusedOffGo passes with js generating; (3) the STEP 4 gate green or reds named as present at BASE.

