# JavaScript carries unbounded text: `[]string`, `[]?string`, `[..N]string`, `[..N]?string` elements and `map[string]V` keys

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.13.1 \"Unbounded text: `[]string` and `map[string]V`\": an element or key with no length bound rides as kind 12 exactly as a bounded one, is never clamped and never dropped for its length, and compares by §2.8's order at any length. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/unboundedtext_test.go TestGoTableUnboundedTextListsAndMapKeys.

THE GAP. After js-carries-bounded-text-lists, refuseTextForms still refuses the unbounded spellings for js (\"unbounded text-list element on field ...\", \"unbounded map key on field ...\", TestUnboundedTextRefusedOffGo).

REGISTER, DO NOT EDIT THE CENTRAL REFUSAL. schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries (a true need of this card) moved every \"Go carries it first\" decision into one list per target: compiler/carries.go's closed key set, and compiler/carries_js.go holding ONE init() with `registerCarries(\"js\", ...)`. Carry the construct in the JS emitter, then add the key `unbounded-text` to that one call in compiler/carries_js.go; that one line is the whole compiler change (compiler/generate.go, refuseTextForms and refuseOptionalMaps are not edited, and the TestXRefusedOffGo tests already ask carries(lang, key), so they now expect js to generate while every other non-Go target still refuses by name). compiler/carries_js.go is on this card's NEW: line because it arrives with the forward merge, not at BASE's tip; it is the only compiler/ file this card edits.

THE TASK. Carry the spellings on the variable wire and the JSON text (map key order by §2.8 at any length, a nested map's key included), and in the view's descriptor (Unbounded true, UnboundedContainer false for the text element and key, as the oracle states).

