# JavaScript: a fixed-form count or text length past its bound refuses by name

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.4 (THE RECORD; the plan's `count` and `text` ops) and docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §4.5, commit 4edb98c8a: a count past the PLAN's bound refuses `count_over_bound` and a text length past the plan's cap refuses `length_over_bound`, both checked before any destination byte is written so REFUSE stays total. The ranged-scalar clamp (§4.6) is unchanged. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/fixedbound_test.go TestFixedFormCountAndLengthOverBoundRefuseByName (identity and compiled lineage plans).

THE GAP AT BASE. internal/codegen/jstable/fixedruntime.go TableFixedOpCount (`else if (v > size) { v = size; report.clamped++; }`) and TableFixedOpText (`else if (v > cap) { v = cap; report.clamped++; }`) clamp; TableFixedRefusal has no CountOverBound or LengthOverBound value and TableFixedRefusalName no such names.

THE TASK. Add CountOverBound and LengthOverBound to TableFixedRefusal and to TableFixedRefusalName (`count_over_bound`, `length_over_bound`), replace both clamps with the refusal on the identity and the compiled plan paths and in the pre-scan, so a refused load has written no destination byte (the existing fixedversioning_refuse_writes_nothing_test.go must stay green). Rewrite the existing clamp-behaviour tests in this package (fixedversioning_count_clamp_ends_test.go, fixedversioning_writer_bound_count*_test.go and any other that asserted the clamp) to the refusal, as GO TIP rewrote Go's.

THE TESTS. TestJsFixedCountAndLengthOverBoundRefuseByName (new) ports the oracle's cases: an older writer's layout with a wider count and a wider string, read by a narrower reader, on the identity and the compiled lineage plans; each asserts -1, the name, and that the destination values are untouched, with Go's answer taken from the Go leg on the same files. Red at BASE (the JS read clamps).

