# JavaScript: every FixedLoad refusal carries its name, framing damage included

THE RULE. docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.3 and docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §11 (refused by name), §21.3: every refusal of `<Name>FixedLoad` has a name equal to one of the exported reason spellings, and the framing-damage returns keep `malformed` set beside the name. Go's set at d808c3f54 (internal/codegen/gotable/fixedruntime.go TableFixedReason*): previous_form, message_form_as_file, newer_form, layout_malformed, layout_unknown, layout_newer (reserved: no load answers it), layout_unsupported, layout_record_too_large, plan_too_large, batch_too_large, no_layout, text_ill_formed, truncated, reserved_not_zero, count_over_bound, length_over_bound. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/fixedrefusalnames_test.go TestFixedLoadNamesEveryRefusal.

THE GAP AT BASE. internal/codegen/jstable/fixedmodule.go's emitted FixedLoad returns `report.malformed = true; return -1;` with NO name for an empty input (line 342), a short header (354), a nonzero reserved byte (356) and a ragged tail (424); and an unknown header hash answers `layout_newer` (line 373, TableFixedRefusal.LayoutNewer) where Go answers `layout_unknown` and keeps layout_newer reserved. TableFixedRefusal has no Truncated, ReservedNotZero or LayoutUnknown.

THE TASK. Add LayoutUnknown, Truncated and ReservedNotZero to TableFixedRefusal and TableFixedRefusalName (fixedruntime.go, read here; the enum lines are inside this card's need on js-fixed-count-and-length-over-bound-refuse-by-name, which adds two values first: take its numbering, append yours), name every framing-damage return (`truncated` for empty, short header and ragged tail; `reserved_not_zero` for the reserved bytes) with malformed kept, and answer `layout_unknown` (hash on the report, nothing else) for a hash no lineage entry holds, keeping LayoutNewer exported and unanswered. If fixedruntime.go must change beyond the enum and its name switch, it is inside PATHS by this card's need; name the lines in the report.

THE TESTS. TestJsFixedLoadNamesEveryRefusal (new) is the oracle's table of cases over `fixed table Point { x int32 = 1  y int32 = 2 }` (previous_form, message_form_as_file, newer_form, layout_malformed, plan_too_large, batch_too_large, no_layout, the three truncated shapes, reserved_not_zero, layout_unknown with its hash), files saved by the Go leg, each asserting -1, the name and malformed exactly as Go's report. Red at BASE.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

