# JavaScript: a plain float's -0 rides by bit pattern, and a NaN or infinity is named non_finite and refused by the strict read

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.3 \"A PLAIN FLOAT'S SPECIAL VALUES TAKE ONE RULE, IN EVERY FORM\" (and its table): default ELISION COMPARES BIT PATTERNS, so a -0 under a +0 default rides (and +0 under a declared -0 default), at every elision (a scalar field, a [N] array left off, an enum-keyed slot) in the variable and the message forms; a NaN or an infinity rides the binary forms bit for bit, the tolerant read lands it and counts nothing but NAMES the field in the report's reason as `non_finite: <Table>.<field>` (first name wins), and the strict read refuses it with `non_finite`. The fixed form carries it whole and names nothing. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/floatspecial_test.go TestGoPlainFloatSpecialValuesAgreeAcrossForms (four schemas: fs, fsFlat, fsKeyed, fsNeg).

THE GAP AT BASE. internal/codegen/jstable/variableruntime.go TableVariableWriteField elides a float with `Math.fround(val) !== Math.fround(fd.def)` / `val !== fd.def`, so -0 under a +0 default is ELIDED (JavaScript's !== says -0 === 0); `grep -rn non_finite internal/codegen/jstable` finds nothing.

THE TASK. Compare float defaults by bit pattern at every elision in the variable writer (scalar, [N] all-default, keyed slot: variablearms.go TableVariableElemIsDefault) and in the message writer (messagebatch.go); name `non_finite: <Table>.<field>` on the variable and message tolerant reads (the plain strict reads, from this card's needs, then refuse it, and report.err() answers `non_finite`); leave the fixed form as it is. The text writer already refuses a non-finite float (ToJson null): keep it.

THE TESTS. TestJsPlainFloatSpecialValuesAgreeAcrossForms (new) runs the oracle's four schemas: for -0 and +0 under each default the wire length and bytes equal Go's (the elision), the read lands the same bits; for each NaN payload and both infinities the tolerant read lands the bits with the same reason Go names and the strict read refuses with non_finite as Go's does, in the variable and the message forms. Red at BASE (the -0 wire is shorter than Go's).

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

