# JavaScript: every table carries SaveText and LoadText, canonical base64 over the binary wire

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.8: EVERY TABLE HAS BOTH text carriers. `<Name>SaveText` writes the wire `<Name>Save` writes as CANONICAL base64 (standard alphabet, padded, pad bits zero, no whitespace); `<Name>LoadText(text, report)` IS THE STRICT READ for both classes: a text whose CR/LF-stripped form decodes but is not exactly canonical is `base64_not_canonical`, every other failure `base64_damaged`, a decoded wire the binary reader refuses keeps that reader's own refusal, and a read whose report holds an error refuses whatever the tolerant load answered. Both suffixes are in §11's claimed list. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/base64canonical_test.go TestGoLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 (the fuzz repro `AQAAAAAAAAAAAB==`). The JSON half (bytes fields inside a JSON text) is schema-go-json-base64-canonical, still WORKING on schema-go: not this card.

THE GAP AT BASE. `grep -rn \"SaveText\\|LoadText\" internal/codegen/jstable` finds nothing: the JS leg has no text carrier at all.

THE TASK. Emit `<Name>SaveText(value)` and `<Name>LoadText(text, report)` for every variable root (over Save and the strict Load) and every fixed-class root (over FixedSave and the strict FixedLoad, value shape as §16.8 states for the fixed class), the decoder written to refuse non-canonical text by name before decoding; claim the two names in the module's claimed-name check the way the other suffixes are claimed (internal/tablenames if this leg's claim list lives there: it is outside PATHS, so put that one-line diff in the report as PATHS-PROPOSED if TestJsTableModuleScopeNamesAreClaimed goes red).

THE TESTS. TestJsLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 (new) uses tables/examples/Tables.schema as the oracle does: the fuzz repro and the oracle's other cases (pad bits set, CR/LF inside, inner `=`, a missing pad, a byte outside the alphabet) answer the same name Go's LoadText answers, and SaveText of the oracle's values equals Go's SaveText text byte for byte. Red at BASE (no such function).

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

DONE-WHEN: (1) TestJsLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 passes and fails at BASE; (2) `grep -c LoadText internal/codegen/jstable/variableform.go` is 0 at BASE, positive at the head; (3) the STEP 4 gate green or reds named as present at BASE.

