THE TASK. Emit, from a new internal/codegen/jstable/testgen.go, `<Base>Table.gen.test.mjs` per file using node's built-in test runner (node:test, node:assert) and the generated modules only, covering what Go's testgen covers for each root; let cmd/schema's testgen accept --lang js; add a make target in make/js.mk that runs testgen over tables/examples and runs the result under node.

THE TESTS. TestJsTestgen (new): testgen over tables/examples writes files that pass under node, and a sabotaged generated module (one byte of a Load flipped in memory, the way the negative controls in this package sabotage) makes them fail; the case list per table matches Go's testgen's for the same unit. Red at BASE.

