# JavaScript: a JSON string that decodes to U+0000 in text storage refuses the read as text_holds_zero

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.3 \"A ZERO IN TEXT TAKES ONE RULE IN EVERY FORM: NO READ STORES IT\": a JSON string the read would PLACE in text storage (a string(N), *string, wstring(N) value, a text-list element, a map key) that decodes to U+0000 refuses the read: FromJson returns false (null here), the report is malformed (one event, one malformed) and the reason reads `text_holds_zero: <Table>.<field>` for the innermost field; a string the read only SKIPS (an unknown key's value) is not the event; a \\u0001 reads clean. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/textzero_test.go TestGoTextZeroByteTakesOneRuleInEveryForm.

THE GAP AT BASE. `grep -rn text_holds_zero internal/codegen/jstable` finds nothing: the JS text reader stores a \\u0000 into a string field, which its own Save then writes as a wire the strict reader calls malformed.

THE TASK. In the text reader, refuse a decoded U+0000 placed in a string(N), *string, wstring(N) or a string map key, with malformed and the reason naming the innermost field (this card's need, js-plain-float-special-values-take-one-rule, adds the report's reason channel to the variable read first; text-list elements join when the text-list cards land, which will call the same check). Leave skipped values alone.

THE TESTS. TestJsTextZeroByteTakesOneRuleInEveryForm (new) runs the oracle's rows the JS leg can declare today (string(8), *string, map[string(8)]int32 key, wstring(8), a nested type's string(8), map[int32]int32 key; the timestamp, text-list and unbounded-key rows are skipped by name until those constructs are carried) with \\u0000 at the front, middle and end, asserting the refusal, malformed and the reason equal Go's, and the \\u0001 control reading clean. Red at BASE.

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

DONE-WHEN: (1) TestJsTextZeroByteTakesOneRuleInEveryForm passes and fails at BASE; (2) `grep -c text_holds_zero internal/codegen/jstable/variableruntime.go` is 0 at BASE, positive at the head; (3) the js json-read and json-hostile surfaces unchanged or better; (4) the STEP 4 gate green or reds named as present at BASE.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
