# JavaScript: the field descriptor carries the exact integer range, the wide raw range and UnboundedContainer

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §8.1: a ranged integer field carries its EXACT range beside the double pair (int64 columns for signed, uint64 for unsigned and bits(N), the implied range for bits(N)), a wide-kind field carries its frac bits and its exact raw range, and a map or an unbounded array carries `UnboundedContainer` true with array_bound 0 (the ONE TELL that tells \"no bound\" from a bound of 2^31 - 1), §2.9. Oracles: internal/codegen/gotable/exactrange_test.go TestGoExactIntegerRangeBounds (the descriptor half: RangeIntMax 9007199254740993 exact, an int128 carrying no int64 pair) and internal/codegen/gotable/unboundeddescriptor_test.go TestGoUnboundedDescriptorIsExplicit (the descriptor half).

THE GAP AT BASE. internal/codegen/jstable/view.go's field descriptor (`{ name, json, id, typeName, kind, shape, bound, arrayBound, isArray, counted, optional, isPointer, ... }`, line 302 and its frozen twin at 449) carries no range column of any kind and no unboundedContainer.

THE TASK. Add, in JavaScript's spelling (camelCase, BigInt for the exact 64-bit and 128-bit values, null where the declaration bounds nothing): rangeMin/rangeMax (the double pair), rangeIntMin/rangeIntMax or rangeUintMin/rangeUintMax (exact), fracBits and the wide raw range (wideMin/wideMax as BigInt), and unboundedContainer, to both descriptor forms, values computed by the same ir helpers gotable/view.go uses so the two legs cannot disagree. Keep every existing column.

THE TESTS. TestJsViewExactRangesAndUnboundedContainer (new) generates the two oracle schemas (`fixed table Big` with the 2^53 + 1 bounds; `table Root` with maps, []int32, []string(8), [..4]int32, []string, map[string]int32) for both legs, prints every field's columns from Go's TableFields and from the JS descriptors, and asserts they match column for column. Red at BASE (no such columns). The JSON half of exactrange (FromJsonTolerant clamping at 9007199254740993 exactly) is checked in the same test against Go's answer; if JS's text read already clamps exactly, say so; if not, fix it here (variableruntime.go is outside PATHS: put the diff in the report as PATHS-PROPOSED).

THE ORACLE. schema-go at d808c3f54 (merged into this base by js-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f) is the expected answer for every case; never write spec text, and never take an expected answer from this leg's own output. Get the Go answer the way internal/codegen/jstable/cardsretain_test.go goRetainedSave does: generate the SAME schema with internal/codegen/golang and internal/codegen/gotable into t.TempDir(), run a small Go driver there with `go test -count=1`, and read its printed answers (wire bytes as hex, the report's counters and reason); or, where the rule lives in an engine package (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext), call the engine directly as textdifferential_test.go does. The JavaScript side runs the generated module in node through jsNode(t), exactly as the existing tests in this package do. Copy the oracle test's schema and cases (named below) so the two legs answer the same inputs.

DONE-WHEN: (1) TestJsViewExactRangesAndUnboundedContainer passes and fails at BASE; (2) `grep -c unboundedContainer internal/codegen/jstable/view.go` is 0 at BASE, positive at the head; (3) the STEP 4 gate green or reds named as present at BASE; (4) generated/js*/ View modules that moved are named.

