THE TASK. Enforce the total in the text-list save, the wire read and the JSON read. The new test runs the refusal test's four L schemas with totals under, at and past N and asserts the Go answers. Register rust as a carrier of this construct: add the key `text-list-total` to rust's registerCarries call in compiler/carries_rust.go, the one per-target file schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries defines (PATHS reaches it as compiler/*_rust.go; nothing else of that card's is edited), so the central refusal in compiler/generate.go (read) (the text list total refusal (TestListTotalBytesRefusedOffGo)) no longer refuses rust and still refuses every other non-Go target: the compiler test that holds the refusal is updated to treat rust as a carrier, the way it treats go.

TESTS. A Go test that only reads the generator's output is a unit test: it uses no real time, sockets, network or outside services. A test that compiles or runs Rust (rustc, cargo) is a functional test: it skips by name when rustc is absent and SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS is unset, fails by name when SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1, and runs on the bench with that variable set, so it never passes on a SKIP. Use the leg's existing harness: the rusttable functional-test pattern (a generated crate built with cargo beside a Go oracle, as retainroots_test.go and messageform_batch_test.go do) and the conformance driver test/conformance/rust/src/main.rs where a surface answers; never a new harness.

