# Rust: a deprecated enum variant reads as the field default and is refused on write

RULING (Glenn, 2026-10-18): \"If it's possible to implement, then implement it!\" Enum variants may be deprecated in place (`| deprecated`), one way only. The standard (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md, card spec-enum-variant-deprecated-in-place) and the Go reference (cards schema-go-enum-variant-deprecated-front-end and schema-go-enum-variant-deprecated-codegen) define it; this port matches Go.

PRECONDITION. The front end (parser, ir Variant.Deprecated, check, lock) is shared and lands on sprint/schema-go. If BASE's ir has no Variant.Deprecated, stop at once with Verdict: HOLD, not-done naming the forward-merge of sprint/schema-go into sprint/schema-rust that is owed; write nothing.

THE TASK. In the Rust table emitter and runtime: a reader meeting a deprecated variant's id, on every form this port carries (id-table wire, form 3, message form, JSON/text where carried), yields the field's declared default (elements: the element default) and does not count unknown; every writer this port has refuses a value holding a deprecated variant with invalid_value, naming <Table>.<field>; the variant's constant stays, marked deprecated in the language's idiom.

TEST, opening with t.Parallel(), under the port's house pattern (a generated unit run in a t.TempDir()): TestDeprecatedVariantReadsDefaultWriteRefused: a wire written with the variant live reads the default once it is deprecated; each writer refuses; REVERSED WITNESS: the same wire read with the variant live yields the variant. Where Go's reference test gives bytes, this port's reads agree with them.

DONE-WHEN: the test RUNs and PASSes at head (red at BASE: no tests to run) for every form the port carries, with its reversed witness; the port's gate passes or its only reds are named as red at BASE.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache: keep it. Check the PRECONDITION.
STEP 2. Red first: write the test, run it, keep its failing line.
STEP 3. Make it pass in the files PATHS names, citing the section of docs/SPEC-TABLES.md from each function that implements a rule.
STEP 4. Run the gate: go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/rusttable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/ and read the last line of each. When a test fails, name its file and say whether your work changed it or it is red at BASE, and report that line first.
