# The Rust fixed load names every refusal, count_over_bound and length_over_bound included (port to the standard, family: bounds, refusal-names)

USE CASE (Glenn, 2026-10-18): \"We do all features across all languages.\" The Rust leg reaches schema-go's behaviour at GO TIP for this feature, with the same answers on the same inputs.

THE STANDARD AND THE ORACLE. The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md as rust-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f brought them onto BASE from sprint/schema-go (d808c3f54, GO TIP, or the later commit that card merges); schema-go's behaviour at GO TIP is the oracle for every expected answer. Expected answers come from the Go side and never from a hand reckoning: the engine packages (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext, internal/rfc3339) where they answer the case, else the generated Go of the same unit through gotable (the Go test named under THE RULE shows the probe), its answers pinned in the new test as literals with a comment naming the Go test they came from. Write no spec text: a gap or a contradiction in the standard goes in the report, quoted.

THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.4 (a count or length past the field's own bound is a NAMED REFUSAL, count_over_bound / length_over_bound, checked before any destination byte is written; the plan table rows `count` and `text`) and docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.3 (every refusal of the fixed load has a name, the four framing-damage returns included, which keep malformed set beside it). Go's exported set at GO TIP (internal/codegen/gotable/fixedruntime.go, TableFixedReason*): previous_form, message_form_as_file, newer_form, layout_malformed, layout_unknown, layout_newer (reserved), layout_unsupported, layout_record_too_large, plan_too_large, batch_too_large, no_layout, text_ill_formed, truncated, reserved_not_zero, count_over_bound, length_over_bound. Oracle: TestFixedLoadNamesEveryRefusal (gotable/fixedrefusalnames_test.go), TestCountOverBoundCompiled and gotable/fixedbound_test.go, commit 4edb98c8a.

THE TASK. In fixedruntime.go: the plan's count op refuses count_over_bound and its text op refuses length_over_bound past the plan's bound instead of clamping (fixedruntime.go:1390 and :1613 clamp today); add TableFixedReason values for every Go name the enum lacks (truncated, reserved_not_zero, count_over_bound, length_over_bound, and the hash refusals no_layout and layout_unknown, which Go names where the leg says no_block / layout_newer), keeping the leg's existing finer layout_* names that Go's §3.4 table also names; every framing-damage return sets its name beside malformed. Rename only where the Go name differs and say in the pull request which old spelling went and every caller updated. The new test is the Go test's case list, one case per name, over the same `fixed table Point { x int32 = 1; y int32 = 2 }` and the same forged files, plus the two bound cases of fixedbound_test.go, each asserting the Go reason and -1.

