THE TASK. In fixedform.go emit the plain fixed load over a _tolerant twin and refuse on the report's clamped or kind_mismatch, resetting the destination; in messagebatch.go the same for the message read. The reason a caller reads is the report's (the err() rust-plain-variable-read-is-strict adds for the message form's TableReport; the fixed form's TableFixedReport answers through its own refused/reason pair). Register new names in internal/tablenames/rust.go. The new test forges the older-layout file the Go fixed subtest forges (n float32 under a reader declaring n int32) and the float32-to-int32 message pair, and asserts the Go answers: -1 and reset values from the plain load, the recovered value and counts from the twin.

