THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5, the bullets \"The STRICT read\" and \"THE PLAIN NAME IS THE STRICT READ; THE TOLERANT READ HAS A NAME OF ITS OWN\", and §11 (the default read refuses at every meaning boundary; writers are strict). Every generated variable read a caller reaches by its plain name (the region load, the builder load and the JSON read, <name>_load, <name>_load_builder where the leg has one, <name>_from_json) refuses whatever the strict read refuses (malformed, clamped, kind-mismatched, unknown form, wire-damaged) and hands back no recovered value; the tolerant read keeps its old signature and answers under the twin name <name>_load_tolerant / <name>_from_json_tolerant; and a <name>_read_strict per root answers the root or one typed reason. TableReason gains Malformed, Clamped and KindMismatch, appended and never renumbered, spelled malformed, clamped and kind_mismatch, and TableReport gains err(), answering the reason for every counter the strict read refuses and None for unknown, widened or retained alone. Oracle: TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict (internal/codegen/gotable/strictdefault_test.go, its variable subtest) and commits 61105d0b1, 1f53ff49d, f995112ac, bcff9c99e, 2c0700baa. The retain family keeps its behaviour (§6.5's named follow-on). The fixed and message reads are rust-plain-fixed-and-message-read-is-strict's, not this card's.

THE TASK. In variablecodec.go rename the emitted whole-file read (its doc line at variablecodec.go:1382 calls it \"the tolerant read of a whole file\") to the _tolerant twin and emit the plain name over it, deciding on this read's report alone; in variabletext.go do the same for the JSON read (variabletext.go:1412); emit <name>_read_strict per root; append the three reasons to TableReason and add TableReport::err() in message.go's tableReportRust; register each new exported item in internal/tablenames/rust.go (TestRustTableRuntimeNamesAreClaimed holds it both ways). Callers inside the leg (the conformance driver's report surface, the wire fuzzer) that need the counters call the tolerant twin by name. The new test drives one unit, the variable subtest's (n int32 = 1 | min = 0, max = 10), through a clamped, a kind-mismatched, a malformed and a clean wire, each built by internal/tablewire, and asserts the plain read refuses with the Go reason, the tolerant twin returns the value with the Go counters, and read_strict answers the same reason.

