# C# generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers

WHY. The Java SpotBugs lens (card schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate, triage list triage-findings-medium-unfiltered.xml in its receipts) found 512 real MS_PKGPROTECT findings: generated fixed-table classes expose public static arrays (layout, defaults, dest, known and the like) whose elements any caller can overwrite, corrupting the decode tables for the whole process. Test code in other packages reads these arrays today. Hot read path stays zero-allocation: the generated code reads its own private table directly; only outside callers go through an accessor.

THE TASK. In internal/codegen/cstable/fixedform.go emit each table as private static readonly (or internal when another generated class in the same assembly needs it, never public). Byte tables (layout, guard pool) are exposed to outside callers only as a public static ReadOnlySpan<byte> property or method; object tables (Dst, Cover, Known, LineagePlans) only as a read-only view (ImmutableArray, or an IReadOnlyList over the private array) whose element objects have no public setters. The generated code reads the private arrays directly. Update the test readers named in PATHS (the Go tests whose embedded C# probes and regexes read FixedLayout and friends, e.g. hashof_oracle_test.go's csLayoutRe) to the new spelling. Regenerate any committed generated tree.

TEST (red at BASE): TestCsFixedTablesPrivate generates a fixed table for a probe schema and asserts the generated source has no public mutable array of those tables; with dotnet present it compiles a probe that tries to write an element of each table from another class and expects a compile error, and that a decode of the same bytes is unchanged after the probe mutates what the accessor returned. It skips by name without dotnet and fails by name under SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1, as its neighbours do.

DONE-WHEN: TestCsFixedTablesPrivate is red at BASE (line kept) and green; go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/cstable/ ./internal/ci/ is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE; report the grep that shows no public static mutable array of the six names remains in the generated output.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; keep the GOCACHE JOB.md names. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names.
STEP 2. RED FIRST at BASE: write the test (see TEST), run it, keep the failing line; it must fail on the rule (a caller can mutate or reach the table and change decoding), not on a build error.
STEP 3. Fix the generator, regenerate, update every test reader to the accessor. Never hand-edit generated files.
STEP 4. Gate: run the named packages, read each last line, report a red as yours or present at BASE.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer; the finish JOB.md names ends the card.
