# nightly fuzzing (cs port of schema)

NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the cs port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: SharpFuzz (AFL-based). Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Instrument the generated assembly with SharpFuzz and drive it with AFL++.

