# cs port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (cs port of schema)

Denial-of-service hardening for the cs port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>.

