# The remaining 64-bit sites in the generated Dart are unsafe under dart2js: union int64 arms, block/home and wide fixed forms lose or corrupt the high bytes between 2^32 and 2^53

SCOPE (coordinator, 2026-10-19, re-scoped in flight). The putU64/readU64/_signExtend codec fix is kept and verified in schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential (d861a246); this card does NOT redo it and lands after it. Dart's shifts and bit operators are the 32-bit JavaScript operators on the web, so any shift of 32 or more, or a bit operation on a value that can exceed 2^31, corrupts under dart2js. This card owns the other sites.

THE SITES, each REAL and owned here: (a) internal/codegen/darttable/wireunion.go:624, `raw |= p.readByte() << (8 * b)`, widths up to 8: a union 64-bit integer arm loses bytes 4 to 7 on the web. (b) The emitter source that produces `lo |= v << 32` in the generated block/Render.dart and blockhome/Data.dart. (c) The emitter source that produces `(bits & 0x80000000) << 32` in the generated wide/WideFixed.dart. (d) EVERY OTHER SITE the full grep turns up: run grep over internal/codegen/darttable (emitters) and the generated Dart trees for shifts by 32 or more, `|=` with a shift, `<<` and `>>` and `&` and `|` on a value that can exceed 2^31, and paste the grep output itself in the report (not prose), then list each hit as REAL (fixed here) or NOT (cannot exceed 32 bits, or already exact), file and line. A hit found by this grep that is in putU64, readU64 or _signExtend is the differential card's, listed as such.

THE TASK. (1) For each REAL site, a web-exact form: arithmetic exact on both targets (multiplication and division or modulo by 2^32 and by powers of two, or a split into two 32-bit halves each combined with exact arithmetic), no shift of a value that may exceed 32 bits and no bitwise operator on one; the VM bytes for every value that was right stay identical. A value above 2^53 - 1 that cannot be held exactly on the web is refused by name on the web path (the existing refusal enum, no new member; strict write, accepting read only when near), never corrupted; the VM keeps all 64 bits. The rule is already stated by the differential card's standard commit; if it is not on the base when you start, state it in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md in a commit of its own first. (2) Differential lane values, each RED at BASE and GREEN at head, compared VM against dart2js, bytes and read-back: a union with an int64 arm at 2^32+5, 2^40+3 and 2^53-1 and at the negative -(2^32+5) (the arm read back through wireunion.go); a block value and a block-home value that reach the `lo |= v << 32` sites with the high word set (2^32+5, 2^53-1); a wide value that reaches the `(bits & 0x80000000) << 32` site with bit 31 set and the high word non-zero. Keep the int64 lane bounds the differential card gives so the values read back unclamped on both runtimes. (3) REVERSED WITNESS PER SITE: in a throwaway copy inside the job put the 32-bit form back at that one site and show the lane goes red naming the value; one control per site (a, b, c, and each site d), recorded in make/negative-controls.json as the lane's other controls are, with the line number kept in the report. (4) AUDIT of other ports: grep the JS port (internal/codegen/jstable) and every other web-targeting emitter for the same 32-bit shift pattern on a value that can exceed 32 bits; list each hit as REAL or NOT, file and line; a REAL one outside Dart is a proposed card (id, stream, one line), not edited here.
REGENERATE. The Dart trees that carry the changed emitters: regenerate with the repository's make targets (find them in make/dart.mk) and commit what they write under generated/; after merging the base tip, rerun the IsCurrent-style tests on the merged tree.

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel(), no real time:
- TestDartEmittedSitesAreWebExact, internal/codegen/darttable/wirewebexactsites_test.go: pure Go over the emitted Dart text of tables/examples and the block, block-home, wide and union examples: no `<<`, `>>`, `&` or `|` applies to a 64-bit, count or length value in the emitted union read, the block and home lo/hi paths and the wide path, and the web refusal for a value above 2^53-1 is emitted. Red at BASE on each of sites a, b and c.
- The differential lane items of THE TASK (a functional test run by the make target; skipped by name when dart is absent and SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS is unset, failing by name when it is 1).

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/darttable/ -run '^TestDartEmittedSitesAreWebExact$' -v` RUNs and PASSes at head (red at BASE); on the bench the VM-versus-dart2js differential make target exits 0 at head with the new values and was red at BASE on each site (the lines kept); every reversed witness turns it red; `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/darttable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/` is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE; the grep output and the REAL/NOT lists are in the finish.
STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Record BASE_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD). Export GOFLAGS='-mod=readonly -p=4' NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Red first: write the tests TEST and THE TASK name, each opening with t.Parallel(); run each and keep its failing line.
STEP 3. Make them pass in the files PATHS names, citing the section of the standard from each function that implements a rule.
STEP 4. Run the gate: the go test lines of DONE-WHEN, then go test -count=1 -timeout 600s on the other packages DONE-WHEN names, and read the last line of each. When a test fails, name its file and say whether that file was changed by your work (yours) or is unchanged (already red at BASE: run the same test on the unchanged base to say so), and report that line first.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against the BASE: line's branch, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
