WHAT IS THERE: internal/slowtest/slowtest.go Gate (line 68) skips a test unless SCHEMA_SLOW=1 or SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS is set; tools/slowgatescan audits that every make recipe running a gated package sets the variable, and its -coverage mode accounts every gated skip in a `go test -json` transcript. 17 compiler/*_test.go files call exec.Command; at least compiler/tablesccook_test.go (line 201, `exec.Command(\"cc\", ...)`) does so with no slowtest.Gate in the file. No guard in internal/ci today fails a non-gated test that execs a program (search internal/ci and tools/slowgatescan for one first; if one exists, extend it instead of adding the new file, and move the NEW name accordingly in the report).

# `go test ./compiler/` runs ~540 s unloaded and hits the 600 s timeout on a loaded bench

Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19: `go test ./compiler/` takes about 540 s on a quiet bench, at head and at base alike, and hits go test's 600 s timeout on a loaded one; with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 it times out reliably. That breaks the one-minute CI rule: a unit test is logic only, with no programs and no real time.

THE TASK. (1) PROFILE first: on the bench, `go test -count=1 -timeout 1200s -json ./compiler/ > before.json` (no SCHEMA_SLOW) and the same with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 (use -timeout 1800s for the measurement only), and build the table: every test over 1 s, its elapsed time, and whether it execs a program (directly or through a helper) or is pure Go that is slow (big corpus generation, a quadratic check). (2) Every compiler test that compiles or runs generated code in another language (C, C++, C#, Java, Rust/cargo, Dart, Elixir, Lua and the rest) or spawns any toolchain or program moves behind slowtest.Gate as a functional test, OR is split into a fast pure-Go assertion (over the generated text, the IR, or the compiler's result) plus a gated run of the program: the property that needs the program stays tested, under the gate. A pure-Go test that is slow is made fast without losing what it asserts (a smaller input that proves the same rule, the corpus walked once and shared across subtests), or moved behind the gate with a sentence saying why. Do NOT raise any timeout. Do not change compiler behaviour: only compiler/*_test.go and the test data. (3) Budget: without SCHEMA_SLOW, `go test ./compiler/` finishes in under 60 s on a quiet bench; with SCHEMA_SLOW=1, under 600 s. If the gated half cannot reach 600 s without moving work to another package or a make target outside PATHS, report PATHS-PROPOSED with the split. (4) Every newly gated test must still be run by a SCHEMA_SLOW=1 recipe or CI step: run `go run ./tools/slowgatescan` and `go run ./tools/slowgatescan -coverage before/after transcript` and keep them green (an exception goes in make/slow-gate-exceptions.txt with its reason only if no recipe can run it).

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel(), no real time:
- TestCompilerTestsExecOnlyBehindTheSlowGate, internal/ci/compiler_tests_exec_gated_test.go: pure Go (go/parser over compiler/*_test.go): every Test function that reaches exec.Command, exec.CommandContext, os.StartProcess or syscall.Exec, directly or through a helper in the package (follow calls by name, as a call graph, cutting cycles), reaches slowtest.Gate (or slowtest.ProbeContext's gated helpers) BEFORE the exec on that path; a test that execs without the gate fails BY NAME with the helper chain. Red at BASE (compiler/tablesccook_test.go's cc call is one).
- REVERSED WITNESS in the same file: fixture sources (in the test, as strings): a test that execs through a helper with no gate fails naming both; the same with slowtest.Gate at its top passes; a pure-Go test passes.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '^TestCompilerTestsExecOnlyBehindTheSlowGate$' -v` RUNs and PASSes at head (red at BASE); `time go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./compiler/` finishes under 60 s on a quiet bench and `time SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./compiler/` under 600 s, both green or their only reds named as present at BASE; the report holds the BEFORE and AFTER timing table (test, before s, after s, exec or pure, what was done), with the bench name and its load (uptime) at each run; `go run ./tools/slowgatescan` passes.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Record BASE_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD). Export GOFLAGS='-mod=readonly -p=4' NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
