# The generated fuzz target treats an enum variant reference to a non-variant id-table entry as a crash; the standard says it is legal (unknown, read as None)

Source. schema-go-reader-enum-variant-ref-not-swapped (attempt 4, read OK, 2026-10-19) found its fuzz crashers are \"case B: harness, not reader\". In both crashers (FuzzLoadoutConfigWire, 212 and 422 bytes, prefix 01011e00030e051e0302020204...) the enum variant reference byte at offset 3 names an id-table entry (entry 3) that is a field-name id (`podium` in the 212-byte sample, `grades` in the 422-byte one), not a variant of the enum. The reader resolves by ENTRY, counts one `unknown` and reads the field as None, exactly as docs/SPEC-TABLES.md section 16.11 and section 4 say it should, and it is not silent. The reader is right. The fuzz target's assertion (decodes to a value whose re-encoding is exactly the input, or refused by name) is wrong for this one legal case: the None read re-encodes with a renumbered id table, so the bytes differ although nothing was misread.

THE TASK. (1) Narrow the generated fuzz target's assertion (the emitter that writes Fuzz<Table>Wire, in the files PATHS names) to allow EXACTLY the section 16.11 case and nothing else: an input whose tolerant read has Report.Unknown increased by exactly one, the unknown being an enum variant reference, whose value reads the enum field as None, may differ from its re-encoding; every other non-canonical accept stays a crash, and so does an unknown count above one, any other Report counter set, or a different field changed. Cite section 16.11 from the emitter code and the emitted comment. Add the one-sentence statement of the narrowed assertion to section 16.11 if it does not already say it. (2) Both pinned crashers (the literal hex in wireenumrefsort_test.go, 212 and 422 bytes) are kept as regression seeds in the generated fuzz targets' testdata corpus (the form `go test fuzz v1` that a generated package's testdata/fuzz/Fuzz<Table>Wire/ holds, written by the test in a t.TempDir() run as the testgen card's tests do) and now pass. (3) Reversed witness: a planted reader that SWAPS the variant instead of reporting unknown (the generated read of entry 3 made to resolve to another declared variant of the enum, planted by the test as a text edit of the generated read, the way the testgen card plants a removed bounds check) must still turn the fuzz target red on the same two inputs. A second plant, the reader reading entry 3 as None but leaving Report.Unknown unchanged (silent), must also turn it red.

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel(), no real time:
- TestGoFuzzEnumVariantRefUnknownIsLegal, internal/codegen/gotable/fuzzenumunknown_test.go, through the same generation and run helpers TestGoTestgenFuzzTargets uses: the genuine reader passes both crashers as seeds; the swapping plant is red; the silent plant is red; an unrelated flip (a byte changed in a scalar field that re-encodes differently) is still red. Check the helper's returned error in every call (internal/ci TestGeneratedHelperResultsAreChecked).
RED AT BASE: the two crashers as seeds make the generated Fuzz target fail (\"re-encoding differs from the input\") against the genuine reader.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^TestGoFuzzEnumVariantRefUnknownIsLegal$' -v` RUNs and PASSes at head (red at BASE as above), `SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^TestGoTestgenFuzzTargets$' -v` still PASSes, and `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/tablewire/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/` is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE. Regenerate the Go trees if the emitter's output for them changes (make generated/bench/tables/go/.stamp generated/bench/paired/go/.stamp generated/bench/go/.stamp, and the fuzzunit tree) after merging the base tip, and commit what they write; internal/ci TestGoBenchTreesAreCurrent and TestGoFuzzUnitIsCurrent must pass on the merged tree.
STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Record BASE_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD). Export GOFLAGS='-mod=readonly -p=4' NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
