# javatable tests: javac only in the functional tier, and bounded there

OWNER RULE (Glenn, restated 2026-10-12): \"Anything that uses real time, network calls, external services, sockets -- that's a functional test.\" Unit tests are lightweight and logic only; a test that runs a program belongs in the functional tier.

THE DEFECT (measured 2026-10-18): one `go test ./...` on hulk spawned about 53 javac processes at once, and two runs pushed a 64-core bench to load 1018. Cause, read at BASE (sprint/schema-go): sixteen files in internal/codegen/javatable call javaTools(t) and run exec.Command(javac, ...) / exec.Command(java, ...) with NO slowtest.Gate and NO bound: cardsform_test.go, cardsretain_test.go, fixedform_test.go, fixedform_ragged_tail_test.go, fixedroadmap_t01, t03, t07, t08, t09, fixedversioning_test.go, fixedversioning_refuse_writes_nothing_test.go, fixedversioning_union_unselected_arm_row_test.go, fixedversioning_unknown_census_many_test.go, fixedversioning_unknown_census_test.go, messageform_announce_test.go, variableform_test.go (re-grep `javaTools(t)` and `exec.Command` for the true list at your BASE; fixedroadmap_t15/t17/t19 already sit behind slowtest.Gate and still run javac, so they move too). Many of them are t.Parallel() subtests, and the package is run in parallel with every other package, so the process count is unbounded.

WHAT THIS CARD DOES
1. Every test that executes javac or java moves into files with `//go:build functional` (split a file when it mixes pure-logic tests and javac tests: the pure tests stay untagged and keep running in the default tier; name the moved files *_functional_test.go, git mv where a whole file moves so history follows). The helpers only the javac tests use (javaTools, the Driver sources, the compile-and-run helpers) move with them; a helper both tiers use stays untagged. The pure-Go halves (text, golden, refusal checks) lose nothing.
2. Bound the functional tier. In the new functional_java_test.go (tagged functional) add one process-wide semaphore sized max(1, GOMAXPROCS/4), and route EVERY javac and java execution in the package through one helper that acquires it (so the bound holds across t.Parallel subtests and across top-level parallel tests). Preferred where cheap: compile all sources of a test in ONE javac invocation rather than one per class. A test that holds the semaphore while it only waits on another test deadlocks: acquire around the exec only. Add a functional test that proves the bound (a fake program counter or a recorded peak of in-flight executions never exceeds the cap under 4x cap concurrent callers; no real javac needed for that one).
3. The unit tier spawns no javac. In the new unit_spawns_nothing_test.go (UNTAGGED, t.Parallel()) add TestUnitTierSpawnsNoProgram: it parses every untagged *_test.go and non-test .go file of the package with go/parser (no process, no network) and fails by file and line on any reference to exec.Command, exec.CommandContext, exec.LookPath, os/exec import, or the string \"javac\" in a call position. If the repo already has a unit-lint program-run counter (grep for it first: slowgatescan, internal/slowtest, tools/*lint*), extend that instead and cite it in the report; if none exists, say so in the report. Prove it red at BASE by running it before the move.
4. Keep the slow-gate-coverage accounting true. `make slow-gate-coverage` reads a PLAIN `go test -json ./...` transcript and places each test that skipped at the gate in a bucket; tests behind a build tag no longer appear in that transcript at all, so they would silently fall out of the accounting. Teach the accounting (tools/slowgatescan) to list the functional-tag tests of the package (go list -tags functional / go vet -tags functional, or a source scan of the tag) and require each to be run by a make target or by ci-full.yml with `-tags functional` and SCHEMA_SLOW=1; every make/*.mk line and workflow step that runs `go test` on internal/codegen/javatable and means the javac tests gets `-tags functional` (java.mk ~319 and its siblings, the fourteen proof-wrapped gates), still through test/slowgate/proof, which must still see a named `--- PASS` per gate. Update make/slow-gate-exceptions.txt only with a reason. Add a vet-functional line for the package if the Makefile has one.
5. In the functional tier, run `go test -tags functional` with the package at `-p 1` or rely on the semaphore: state which in the make comment.

DONE-WHEN (each shown with its last output line):
- `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/javatable/` passes and starts zero javac and zero java (show it: run it with a PATH whose javac and java are shims that append a line to a file under the job directory, then assert the file is empty; the shims stay out of the commit).
- TestUnitTierSpawnsNoProgram is RED at BASE and green at head.
- `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s -tags functional ./internal/codegen/javatable/` passes where a JDK exists (on a Linux bench; state which), and the shim run shows peak concurrent javac/java <= max(1, GOMAXPROCS/4).
- `make slow-gate-scan` and `make slow-gate-coverage` pass, and the coverage table in build/slowgate/coverage.tsv still places every moved test in a bucket other than \"run by nobody\".
- `go vet -tags functional ./internal/codegen/javatable/` is clean.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set: keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac. Run the javac tests with a bounded GOMAXPROCS (GOMAXPROCS=8 or less) and never run `go test ./...` at BASE on a shared bench: it is the defect.
STEP 2. Red first: write TestUnitTierSpawnsNoProgram and run it at BASE; it must fail naming the files.
STEP 3. Split and move the tests; add the semaphore helper and its bound test.
STEP 4. Make the unit test green; run the default package tier with the shim PATH.
STEP 5. Wire the make lines, the workflows, the coverage accounting; run the scan and coverage targets.
STEP 6. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall; the pull request is the finish JOB.md names, with the diff stat, what moved, and the gate lines in the body.
STEP 7. End as JOB.md says.

