# a JSON integer field is read exactly, never through float64, in both Go engines

OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" The standard states the rule first; then Go is fixed and a test proves it. No other language's emitter, runtime or driver is edited.
Source: the comprehensive spec-vs-Go review of 2026-10-18 (Glenn: \"do a *comprehensive* spec review vs. the golang implementation and make sure they match\"). A cold reader found this row at sprint/schema-go d808c3f54, with the Go file and line it read; the coordinator's ruling (under Glenn's delegation, 2026-10-18) follows the reviewer's recommendation: fix Go; the spec rule is right, and Go already reads map keys exactly. Line numbers are as read at d808c3f54 and may have moved a few lines; find the code by the name given.

THE TASK. §16.2: a fractional value in an integer field is `kind_mismatch`, and an integral value lands as itself. Both Go JSON readers send a token with a fraction or exponent through float64, so `1.0000000000000001` lands as 1 with nothing counted and `9007199254740993.0` lands as 9007199254740992. Read every integer field with the exact digit reading the map key already has (interpretIntegerExact), in the generated walk and in tabletext. The tests (one per engine, the second TestTextIntegerFieldReadsExactly in internal/tabletext) feed an int64 field `9007199254740993.0` (lands 9007199254740993), `1e2` (lands 100), `1.0000000000000001` and `1.5` (each `kind_mismatch`, field unchanged), and `-0.0` (lands 0), and require the two engines to land the same bytes and counters.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^TestJsonIntegerFieldReadsExactly$' -v` RUNs and PASSes at head, and is red at BASE (no RUN line, or the failing line the task names, kept in the report); `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/tabletext/ -run '^TestTextIntegerFieldReadsExactly$' -v` also RUNs and PASSes at head and is red at BASE. The gate of STEP 4 is green, or each red in it is shown red at the unchanged BASE.

