# Both JSON readers refuse a lone or out-of-order surrogate escape, by name, instead of replacing it silently with U+FFFD

This card stands on schema-go-jsontestsuite-policy, which lands first: it vendors JSONTestSuite under testdata/jsontestsuite, writes the policy table as SPEC-TABLES 16.11, rewrites 16.3's read rule to a refusal named `string_lone_surrogate: <key>`, and lists in testdata/jsontestsuite/PENDING.tsv the 10 files this card closes. Read those at your BASE before writing anything; the reason text and the key spelling are 16.11's, not this brief's.

RED AT BASE (sprint/schema-go @ f820a0c1f566, hetzner1, 2026-10-17). A probe through runGenerated with `fixed table Root { s string(16)  w wstring(16) }`, and the same texts through the engine's Model.Read:
- GEN `{\"s\":\"\\ud800\"}` ok=true s=efbfbd malformed=false reason=\"\"
- GEN `{\"s\":\"\\udd1e\\ud834\"}` ok=true s=efbfbdefbfbd malformed=false
- GEN `{\"w\":\"\\ud800\"}` ok=true w=[fffd] malformed=false
- ENGINE: all three ok=true, Malformed false, Reason empty.
- The policy card's JSON-layer probe accepted, in both readers, i_object_key_lone_2nd_surrogate, i_string_1st_surrogate_but_2nd_missing, i_string_1st_valid_surrogate_2nd_invalid, i_string_incomplete_surrogate_and_escape_valid, i_string_incomplete_surrogate_pair, i_string_incomplete_surrogates_escape_valid, i_string_invalid_lonely_surrogate, i_string_invalid_surrogate, i_string_inverted_surrogates_U+1D11E and i_string_lone_second_surrogate.
- `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^TestGoJsonRefusesLoneSurrogate$' -v` and `./internal/tabletext/ -run '^TestEngineStringRefusesLoneSurrogate$'` print `[no tests to run]` (both new).

THE TASK. In both readers (the engine's \\u handling in scanUnit, scanString and scanWString in internal/tabletext/read.go, using hex4; the emitted scanText's escape branch in internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, and wstring.go if the wide read pairs units there), at every string site (a field value, a key, a skipped value, a wstring), a `\\u` escape in D800..DBFF not followed at once by a `\\u` escape in DC00..DFFF, or a `\\u` escape in DC00..DFFF not preceded by such a high half, makes the read return false with Malformed set and Reason exactly as 16.11 spells it. The pairing logic that today chooses U+FFFD already sees both halves, so the change is one branch per site: no new allocation, no new pass, and AllocsPerRun stays 0 wherever an existing test asserts it. Then delete the 10 lines naming this card from testdata/jsontestsuite/PENDING.tsv.
- Existing tests that pin the old silent replacement ON READ (16.5's hostile battery row \"a lone surrogate\") change to the refusal (tests are inside PATHS); 16.5's WIDE TEXT rows that build an unpaired surrogate IN CODE and pin the WRITER's U+FFFD stay as they are. Name every test you change in the report.
- Regenerate the Go bench trees after changing the emitted source: `make generated/bench/tables/go/.stamp generated/bench/paired/go/.stamp generated/bench/go/.stamp` (internal/ci TestGoBenchTreesAreCurrent checks them), and commit what it writes.
- Raw invalid UTF-8 BYTES are the sibling card schema-go-json-refuses-invalid-utf8: do not change the byte-decode path here.

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel():
- TestGoJsonRefusesLoneSurrogate, internal/codegen/gotable/surrogaterefusal_test.go, through runGenerated with the unit above: `{\"s\":\"\\ud800\"}`, `{\"s\":\"\\udfaa\"}`, `{\"s\":\"\\ud800abc\"}`, `{\"s\":\"\\ud888ሴ\"}`, `{\"s\":\"\\udd1e\\ud834\"}`, `{\"s\":\"\\ud800\\ud800\\n\"}`, `{\"\\udfaa\":0}` (a key) and `{\"w\":\"\\ud800\"}` each return false with Malformed and Reason starting `string_lone_surrogate`; `{\"s\":\"𝄞\"}` reads clean as F0 9D 84 9E and `{\"w\":\"𝄞\"}` as the units D834 DD1E.
- TestEngineStringRefusesLoneSurrogate, internal/tabletext/surrogaterefusal_test.go: the same rows through Model.Read.

DONE-WHEN: `SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^(TestGoJsonRefusesLoneSurrogate|TestJSONTestSuiteGenerated)$' -v` and `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/tabletext/ -run '^(TestEngineStringRefusesLoneSurrogate|TestJSONTestSuiteEngine|TestJSONTestSuitePolicyWitness)$' -v` show every named test RUN and PASS at head, with no PENDING line naming this card left (red at BASE: the probe lines above and no tests to run); the STEP 5 gate is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE.

