# the string_not_utf8 refusal names the key that held the bytes, and the harness checks the reason, not just `refused`

OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" No other language's emitter, runtime or driver is edited.

Source. The cold read r2 of schema-go-spec-16-3-nul-escape-scope (coordinator, 2026-10-19; receipts kept by the coordinator, not in the job).

THE DEFECT. §16.3 says the refusal's Reason is `string_not_utf8: <key>`, the key whose name or value held the ill-formed bytes, `<root>` only at the top. The generated Go reader writes `string_not_utf8: <root>` at every site (internal/codegen/gotable/json.go:1473). For the hostile row str-illformed-at-bound (`{\"profiles\":[{\"name\":\"aaa...\\xff\"}]}`) the reason must read `string_not_utf8: name`. The MANIFEST comment beside that row repeats the wrong `<root>`, and the harness scores only `refused`, so a wrong reason passes.

THE TASK. (1) Fix the Go reader in internal/codegen/gotable/json.go so the reason names the key being read (the key whose value or name held the bytes; `<root>` only for a top-level string with no key), and make internal/tabletext/read.go give the same reason for the same text; regenerate with the repository's make targets and commit what they write under generated/. (2) Correct the MANIFEST comment to `string_not_utf8: name`. (3) The harness checks the reason text for this row from ports that carry string_not_utf8 (the carrying set schema-go-json-hostile-utf8-rows-exempt-unported-legs adds; ports outside it are unaffected): add the expected reason to the row in the data form that card documents, or beside it, and score a carrying port's wrong reason red.

THE TESTS (t.Parallel(), no real time): TestGoJsonUtf8RefusalNamesTheKey in internal/codegen/gotable/utf8reasonkey_test.go, using the package's runGenerated pattern: ill-formed bytes in a field value read `string_not_utf8: <that key>`, in a nested field's value the innermost key, in an object key the key's own (refused) text position as §16.3 says, at the top `<root>`; the same reasons from internal/tabletext. A harness test requiring a go reason of `string_not_utf8: <root>` for str-illformed-at-bound to score red.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^TestGoJsonUtf8RefusalNamesTheKey$' -v` RUNs and PASSes (red at BASE on the `<root>` reason, line kept); `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ ./internal/tabletext/ ./internal/tablepack/ ./test/conformance/harness/` green or reds named as present at BASE; the generated trees are current (the repository's IsCurrent-style tests pass after regeneration).

