# Mutation testing for the Go table leg: the pinned tool, the targets, the nightly report

THE TASK. (1) Choose the tool by trial, not by name: run each candidate on internal/codegen/gotable/messagewrite.go (read) for at most fifteen minutes and record mutants generated, killed, survived, timed out, and minutes; choose the one whose run is reproducible (the same survivors on two runs) and whose test command can be set per target, and say why in tools/mutation/README.md. (2) Pin it in its own module, tools/mutation/go.mod, with a go tool directive (`go get -tool <module>/cmd/<name>@<version>` run inside tools/mutation), so the root go.mod stays free of requirements; run it with `go tool -modfile=tools/mutation/go.mod <name>`. (3) tools/mutation/targets.tsv names each target (file, the test command that kills its mutants, a timeout): the read emitters internal/codegen/gotable/read.go (read) and messageread.go, the write emitters write.go, messagewrite.go and cookwrite.go, and tables/goruntime/goruntime.go (read). Emitter mutants are killed by the generated-unit tests in internal/codegen/gotable (the runGenerated pattern), so each target's command is the package's tests, never a narrower filter that would hide kills; that file is generated (DO NOT EDIT), so its mutants are measured there but any fix belongs to the emitter that writes it. (4) tools/mutation/report.go reads the tool's output and prints one `SURVIVED <file>:<line>:<col> <mutator> <original> -> <mutant>` line per survivor not listed in tools/mutation/equivalent/*.tsv (columns file, line, mutator, original, why; a row whose line no longer holds the original text is reported STALE, never silently kept), then a summary line `mutation targets=<n> mutants=<n> killed=<n> survived=<n> equivalent=<n> timed_out=<n> not_covered=<n> score=<pct>`. (5) make/go.mk gains `mutation-go` (all targets, or MUTATION_FILES=<list>) writing build/mutation/; .github/workflows/mutation-nightly.yml runs it nightly and on workflow_dispatch, uploads build/mutation/ as an artifact and prints the report; never in ci-fast or ci-full. (6) Measure one full run on the bench and record minutes per target in the README; if the whole set does not fit a six-hour job, shard the nightly by target.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./tools/mutation/` (run from tools/mutation if it is its own module) passes, TestReportListsSurvivors covering a canned tool output with one killed, one survived and one equivalent mutant (the equivalent one suppressed), and a STALE equivalent row; `make mutation-go MUTATION_FILES=internal/codegen/gotable/messagewrite.go` runs on the bench and prints the summary line; the workflow parses as YAML and has no push or pull_request trigger; the root go.mod is unchanged; the trial table and the per-target minutes are in tools/mutation/README.md and the pull request; and `/usr/bin/time -v make mutation-go MUTATION_FILES=internal/codegen/gotable/messagewrite.go` (and the full six-target run, if measured) reports \"Maximum resident set size\" under 6 GiB (6291456 kbytes), the line kept in the report.

MEMORY BOUND (attempt 3's child was killed with exit 137, out of memory, on amd-3, amd-1 and vision; the bench sandbox caps a job at 8 GiB). Every mutation run, in make/go.mk and the workflow alike, runs with GOMEMLIMIT=6GiB exported and its test command as `go test -p 1 -parallel 2 -timeout 600s <pkg>`; mutants run serially, or at most 2 at once: set the tool's worker count explicitly (for gremlins `--workers 2` or 1, and `--test-cpu 1`; for go-mutesting its exec runs one at a time), never the CPU-count default. Where the tool spawns one compile or one go test per mutant, cap that concurrency at 2 in the make target (a MUTATION_JOBS ?= 2 variable passed to the tool) and say in the README how the cap is enforced. Run the DONE-WHEN commands one at a time under nice, never two at once, never in the background; if peak RSS still crosses 6 GiB, drop to 1 worker and record it; if it still does, stop with HOLD naming the target and the peak, rather than letting the job be killed.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly holds for the root module; only inside tools/mutation does `go get -tool` write go.mod and go.sum. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. RED AT BASE: `test -e tools/mutation/go.mod || echo missing` prints `missing`.
STEP 3. Run the trial; pin the chosen tool; write TestReportListsSurvivors red first, opening with t.Parallel(), then report.go.
STEP 4. Write targets.tsv, the make target and the workflow; run the DONE-WHEN commands.
STEP 5. Run the gate: go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ and read the last line; then go vet on each package you changed. When a test fails, name its file and say whether that file was changed by your work (yours) or is unchanged (already red at BASE: run the same test on the unchanged base to say so), and report that line first.
STEP 6. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: the member pushes and opens the pull request against the BASE: line's branch from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, the trial table, the first survivors per target, and what was not done.
STEP 7. End as JOB.md says: where JOB.md ends the card with its pull request, that is the end; where it asks for RESULT.md, write it in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report). The report starts with Verdict: LAND or Verdict: HOLD on line 1 and Head: <sha> on line 2.

