THE TASK. Get the survivor list: when tools/mutation/README.md (read) measures this batch at 90 minutes or less, run `make mutation-go MUTATION_FILES=\"tables/goruntime/goruntime.go\"` on the bench; when it measures more, the coordinator adds the newest mutation-nightly run's SURVIVED lines for these files to this card as a SURVIVORS: line before it is dealt, and with neither, stop at HOLD naming it. Take each survivor in file and line order. For each: apply that one mutant by hand to a scratch copy (or with the tool's single-mutant mode), and either (a) write a test that passes at BASE and fails under the mutant, in the batch's new test file, named for the rule the mutant breaks (never for the mutant), opening with t.Parallel(), and say in the report which survivor it kills; or (b) when the mutant cannot change any observable behaviour, add a row to tools/mutation/equivalent/goruntime.tsv (file, line, mutator, original, why), the why a sentence a reader can check against the code, never \"unreachable\" without the reason. A survivor that is a real defect (the mutant's behaviour is what the standard requires, or neither is) is not triaged here: report it with the standard section, as a finding for the coordinator. Change no emitter or runtime source: this card writes tests and notes only. Survivors that do not fit the deadline are listed in the report as not done, with their count; the coordinator cards the rest. tables/goruntime/goruntime.go is generated (DO NOT EDIT) and is in PATHS only to be mutated: never commit a change to it.

