# Go: every spec limit gets an accept test and a refuse test, tied to the enforced constant (go port of schema)

Glenn, 2026-10-18: schema must be bulletproof. A read of the spec limits against the Go code found these gaps; close all of them. (1) blob_cap (2^32-1) is not tied to the check that enforces it at internal/codegen/gotable/unboundedtext.go:122, so a planted `>0xfffffffe` passed the tests: derive the check from the one constant and test both sides. (2) The Go arena size is checked only under SCHEMA_SLOW: make the check run in the normal tier (a pure function over sizes, no allocation of the real arena in a unit test). (3) Add two-way runtime tests (at the limit accepts, one past refuses by its NAME) for: blob_cap; json_max_depth 128 accepts and 129 refuses; message_skip_depth (today only a source-string test pins it); a wrong cook_magic refused in Go; int32_extent_cap at the cap; storage_cap one past; fixed_record_bound accept side; fixed_remap_max accept side; and the text defaults 65536, 8192, 4096 and 65536 at the exact bound (read the spec for which limit each default is). (4) The gate command runs ./test/go-tables from the repo root, which is wrong because it is a separate module (test/go-tables/go.mod): fix it to cd test/go-tables first (see make/go.mk, which already does so for Soak and Fuzz) and prove with a planted failing test in that module that the gate goes red. Each limit gets an accept test and a refuse test, and each test names the constant the code actually enforces (reference it, never a copied literal), so changing the constant moves the test and a planted off-by-one in the check turns exactly one test red.

Files you may touch: the PATHS above, plus the NEW files the card needs (the card's own make file make/schema-go-spec-limits-two-way-bounds.mk (the Makefile includes make/*.mk, so no Makefile edit is needed), its own workflow .github/workflows/schema-go-spec-limits-two-way-bounds.yml (a schedule and workflow_dispatch trigger for nightly parts, push or pull_request for fast parts), and test files; cards share no workflow or Makefile edits so they land independently. When the work needs a file outside PATHS (the port's test tree, generator, fixtures, saved corpus), report PATHS-PROPOSED with the paths and stop that part as not-done). Do not add needs on other cards: this lens stands alone. Worktree: the staged checkout JOB.md names; branch: the card's own; base: sprint/schema-go.
Libraries considered: the Go standard library and the repository's own tools (tools/negativecontrols, tools/slowgatescan, internal/ci) for gates and tests; the checker or fuzzer named above for the analysis itself, installed fleet-wide from its official source; no hand-written reimplementation of any checker.

