# Writing a builder's unlocked root with no arena refuses by name instead of writing zeros

OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15 12:34Z): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" Where this card changes a rule, the rule is written in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md first, in a commit of its own, and Go is then made to match it; no other language's emitter is edited.

Source. The schema Go fuzz campaign (Glenn, 2026-10-17: \"Should we try to fuzz test golang schema implementation more? I'd like to catch anything else NOW vs. after ports.\"), random schemas generated, compiled and driven through every Go read and write path on hetzner and hulk; this card is one minimized finding, confirmed by hand.

RED AT BASE (sprint/schema-go @ caea41783, hulk, 2026-10-17). Unit `table Root { n int32; s *string; xs []int32; names []string(8) }`. A builder filled by RootFromJson from {\"n\":7,\"s\":\"hello\",\"xs\":[1,2,3],\"names\":[\"a\",\"b\"]} (report silent), BEFORE b.Lock():
- RootMeasure(b.GetRoot()) returns 97 and RootSave writes 97 bytes; ReadStrict of that wire gives {\"n\":7,\"s\":\"\",\"xs\":[0,0,0],\"names\":[\"\",\"\"]}: every list element and the blob came out zero or empty, silently.
- the same with &b.Arena passed (RootMeasure(b.GetRoot(), &b.Arena)) gives 104 bytes and the right values; after b.Lock(), RootSave(b.AsConst()) gives the same 104 bytes.
Reported from real use in nova-tools and confirmed here. `go test ... -run '^TestGoWriteOfUnlockedBuilderWithoutArenaRefuses$'` prints no tests to run (new).

THE TASK. When a write (Measure, MeasureReason, Save, SaveText, ToJsonMeasure, ToJson, CookMeasure, the retain and message writes) meets an ARENA-encoded reference (6.3) and was handed no arena to resolve it, it refuses: Measure and Save return -1, the Reason variants return a new named TableRefuseReason (for example `arena_required`), and nothing is written. Find the one place references are resolved on the write side and test the encoding there, so every writer gets it; a locked region's references are unaffected and stay zero-cost. Write the reason into 6.3 (a short sentence, committed first) and the USAGE.md list of refusal reasons, and claim the new reason's Go name the way refusal.go claims its neighbours.

THE TEST, through runGenerated over the unit above: unlocked with no arena, every writer named refuses with the new reason (errors.Is); unlocked with &b.Arena, and locked with none, each writes the 104-byte wire and ReadStrict gives the input values back; a table with no references (`table Root { n int32 }`) writes unlocked with no arena exactly as at BASE.

DONE-WHEN: `SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^TestGoWriteOfUnlockedBuilderWithoutArenaRefuses$' -v` RUN and PASS at head (red at BASE: no tests to run, and the 97-byte line above), and the STEP 5 gate is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE.

