STEP 2. Where THE TASK names a standard change, write it into docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (and docs/USAGE.md where named) and commit that alone, before any code.
STEP 3. Red first: write the test TEST names, opening with t.Parallel(); run the DONE-WHEN command and keep its failing line.
STEP 4. Make it pass in the files PATHS names, citing the section of the standard from each function that implements a rule.
STEP 5. Run the gate: go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/check/ ./internal/tablewire/ ./internal/tabletext/ ./internal/tablepack/ ./internal/ci/ and read the last line of each; then go vet on each package you changed. When a test fails, name its file and say whether that file was changed by your work (yours) or is unchanged (already red at BASE: run the same test on the unchanged base to say so), and report that line first.
STEP 6. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: the member pushes and opens the pull request against the BASE: line's branch from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, the test with what it pins, the red line at BASE and the green line at head, and what was not done.
