COORDINATOR NOTE (2026-10-17, after attempts 1 and 3 ran out the clock without a result): start from the attempt 2 head 58f027dc94a7. The read finding to fix: internal/codegen/gotable/regions.go:191-199 and the tableNumber change (head 58f027dc94a7): the refusal tells an arena-encoded root by ADDRESS, via a process-global registry of every live TableArena (tableArenaRegister in Init, unregister only in Shutdown) scanned under a global RWMutex on every write handed no arena, instead of testing the encoding as THE TASK says. Two defects follow, both reproduced on amd-3 via runGenerated over the card unit, head vs BASE 94b86f1b6c2c: (1) LEAK: an unlocked builder dropped without Shutdown is pinned forever by tableArenaLiveSet; 1000 abandoned RootBuilders after FromJson and runtime.GC twice keep heap_delta_MB=1228.6 at head (two runs), 0.0 at BASE. (2) NOT ZERO-COST: THE TASK requires the locked region path to stay zero-cost, but every locked RootSave(b.AsConst(), buf) now takes the global lock and walks every live arena segment list; with 2000 live unlocked builders a locked RootSave costs 78735/210491/254624 ns/op at head vs 1878/3843/23013 at BASE (loaded bench, three runs; head is 10-100x slower and grows with the number of live builders). Fix: decide by the form in hand, not by address: e.g. an unexported marker or flag the builder sets on arena-encoded storage (or pass the encoding explicitly from GetRoot vs AsConst paths) so tableNumber knows without a global; no global registry, no lock on the write path; add a test that an abandoned builder is collectable and that a locked write does not consult builder state. Everything else held: DONE-WHEN RUN+PASS (0.52s), BASE no tests to run; gate gotable(+SCHEMA_SLOW=1 full run ok 172.7s)/compiler/check/tablewire/tabletext/tablepack/parser/ir/ci all ok; vet 0; gofmt -l empty; go generate 0, git diff --exit-code 0; 442 base-vs-head generations, 0 exit or stderr diffs, 188 differing files all .go (153 the arena_required reason lines, 35 also the registry and edges runtime), cpp 0. Probes, unlocked no arena: Measure -1, MeasureReason -1 arena_required, Save -1 buffer untouched, SaveText arena_required, ToJsonMeasure/ToJson -1 untouched, CookMeasure -1, CookMeasureReason arena_required, MeasureRetain/SaveRetain -1 untouched, tableMessageRegionWrite false (BASE wrote 97 bytes, 92 JSON, 208 cook silently); nested inline table, list of tables, *Inner, map[int32]*string and union-arm-only roots all refuse at head (BASE silently 55/65/25 vs 56/66/73 with arena); with &b.Arena 104 and locked 104 identical, Outer 234 identical; Plain wire byte-identical to BASE. No r1 read finding exists: attempt 1 ended on a deadline harness fault, not a read.
Do not write under /tmp (the sandbox denies it: /tmp/genprobe.schema was refused); use t.TempDir() or the job tmp directory. Run tests with GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2. Commit and push as soon as TestGoWriteOfUnlockedBuilderWithoutArenaRefuses passes, then run the package gate, and write RESULT.md before the deadline even if not done.")
