# A writer's refusal names its reason but not the Table.field it refused at

Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. The C++ deprecated-enum card has deferred its field naming to this card.

THE TASK. (1) The standard first, in its own commit: in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md state once, where the write path's refusals are described (beside §6.5's reasons, or a WRITE paragraph that every construct's WRITE rule cites), that a writer that refuses (Measure / Save / CookMeasure / PackMeasure / FixedSave on an out-of-range, retired, or otherwise invalid value) names BOTH the refusal reason (a member of the one refusal enum) AND the `<Table>.<field>` path it refused at (for a nested value, the path from the root, `<Root>.<field>.<field>`, with `[i]` for an element and `[key]` for a map entry where the writer knows it). One USAGE line. (2) Then Go: extend the *Reason entry points (MeasureReason, CookMeasureReason, PackMeasureReason, FixedSaveReason) so the error they return carries the field path: a small error type in the runtime (for example TableWriteRefusal{Reason TableRefuseReason; Field string}) whose Error() is `<reason>: <Table.field>` and whose Is/Unwrap makes errors.Is(err, TableRefuseInvalidValue) (and every other reason) still hold, so no existing caller breaks. Keep the int64 results and every plain (non-Reason) entry point unchanged; the hot path pays nothing on success (the path is built only on the refusal branch). Regenerate the Go trees and runtime with `make generated/bench/tables/go/.stamp generated/bench/paired/go/.stamp generated/bench/go/.stamp` and the fuzz units as their make target does, and commit what they write. (3) PORT FOLLOW-ONS: each port's reason twin (C, C++, C#, Java, JS, Dart, Elixir, Rust, Lua, Luau, Squirrel) follows on its own card; this card edits no other language. Name that in the report; the C++ deprecated-enum card's field naming is the first of them.

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel(), no real time, through runGenerated behind slowtest.Gate, in internal/codegen/gotable/writerrefusalfield_test.go:
- TestGoWriterRefusalNamesTheField, one subtest per refusal kind the Go writers return today (at least: an out-of-range value under `| min/max` where the writer refuses rather than clamps, a deprecated (retired) enum variant (`invalid_value`, §2.15), a text value over its bound or ill-formed, a nested table's field, an array element and a map entry): each of MeasureReason, and FixedSaveReason for a fixed root, returns an error whose Error() names the reason and the exact `<Table>.<field>` path, and errors.Is(err, <the reason>) holds. Red at BASE (the field is not named).
- REVERSED WITNESS in the same file: a clean value returns a nil error and the same size as the plain Measure; and an error from a refused value does NOT match a different reason under errors.Is.

DONE-WHEN: `SCHEMA_SLOW=1 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ -run '^TestGoWriterRefusalNamesTheField$' -v` RUNs and PASSes every subtest at head (red at BASE); the spec commit precedes the code commit; `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/gotable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/` is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE.

