# Java generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers

WHY. The Java SpotBugs lens (card schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate, triage list triage-findings-medium-unfiltered.xml in its receipts) found 512 real MS_PKGPROTECT findings: generated fixed-table classes expose public static arrays (layout, defaults, dest, known and the like) whose elements any caller can overwrite, corrupting the decode tables for the whole process. Test code in other packages reads these arrays today. Hot read path stays zero-allocation: the generated code reads its own private table directly; only outside callers go through an accessor.

THE TASK. In internal/codegen/javatable/fixedform.go (emitByteConstant for layout and defaults, the dest int[] near it, the known layouts and writer-bounds arrays, and block.go's projectionOffsets) emit every table array as private static final, never public or package-visible to another package. Callers outside get an accessor that returns a copy (clone) or an unmodifiable view; the generated class reads its own array directly with no accessor and no allocation on the read path. Update every test reader that touches these arrays (test/conformance/java/rows/*, test/java-fixedform) to the accessor, and regenerate the committed generated trees if the repository holds any. Where a nested helper class in the same file needs the array, keep it private to the file's outermost class.

TEST (red at BASE): TestJavaFixedTablesPrivate generates a fixed table for a probe schema and asserts on the generated source that no `public static final` or package-level array of layout, defaults, dest, known, writer bounds or projection offsets remains, and, with a JDK present, compiles a probe in another package that tries to assign an element of each table and expects the compile error (no public field) while the accessor's returned copy, once mutated, leaves a second decode of the same bytes unchanged.

DONE-WHEN: TestJavaFixedTablesPrivate is red at BASE (line kept) and green; the existing javatable and java conformance tests are green or their only reds are named as present at BASE; the regenerated tree compiles and the rows tests pass on the accessor; if the SpotBugs gate make target exists at your base (make/schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate.mk), its MS_PKGPROTECT count is 0 over the corpus (report the before and after counts); if it does not yet exist, say so and give the count from the receipt's list instead.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; keep the GOCACHE JOB.md names. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names.
STEP 2. RED FIRST at BASE: write the test (see TEST), run it, keep the failing line; it must fail on the rule (a caller can mutate or reach the table and change decoding), not on a build error.
STEP 3. Fix the generator, regenerate, update every test reader to the accessor. Never hand-edit generated files.
STEP 4. Gate: run the named packages, read each last line, report a red as yours or present at BASE.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer; the finish JOB.md names ends the card.
