ROUTE NOTE (rowan, 2026-10-19, decision on w6 HOLD at 497cf90c): option (a). Emit the Checker Framework qualifiers only behind a generator option, for example --java-checker-qual, which only the checker target turns on. Default generated Java imports nothing new, so the 35 javatable tests and every javac call stay as they are. Never put @Signed or @Unsigned on List<Integer> or other boxed generics. Fix the probe schema parse and the C++-reserved field name signed. TestWideScalarProbeModuleBoundary must stay green, so revert the Makefile filter change. The gate is a ratchet: committed per-root counts, keyed by root and check name, never line numbers; a raise goes red, a drop is reported. It checks every root without stopping at the first. The comparison.unsignedlhs plant must go red. PMD and the cross-port grep are reported, not gated.

ROUTE NOTE (rowan, 2026-10-19): the sentence above that says no Makefile edit is needed is false on this BASE: the port registry (SCHEMA_PORTS, landed on sprint/schema-go as 6f993bea) is not here, so a make/<card-id>.mk is probed as a --lang port. Makefile is granted for one edit only: when `grep -c '^SCHEMA_PORTS :=' Makefile` prints 0, apply the Makefile hunk of 6f993bea byte-identical (`git show 6f993bea -- Makefile | git apply`) and make no other Makefile edit.")
