STEP 1. COUNTER. Build the allocation counter harness first and prove it counts by a planted unbounded allocation.
STEP 2. CASES. One test per hostile shape (huge count, deep nesting, recursion, giant string, many unknown fields), each at the documented factor and depth cap, each failing at BASE if the port is unbounded there (keep the failing lines).
STEP 4. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against sprint/schema-java, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
