# checkJs strict: the cook-write engine uses unknown values without narrowing (~965 findings)

Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. Card schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types (branch sprint/schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types.w1.g1.e21, head 2b130c5e3) brought `tsc --checkJs --strict` over the generated JS corpus from 41,066 findings to 7,642 with JSDoc only; its report (NOT DONE 1) names the groups that remain, all needing real code changes. Card name of the whole: schema-js-checkjs-strict-to-zero, split into one card per group plus a last card that sets the gate's ratchet to 0. This card is one group. Real code changes in the JS emitter and the runtimes it emits are allowed. THE HARD RULE: the wire bytes stay byte-identical.

THE TASK. The emitted cook-write engine (internal/codegen/jstable/cookwrite.go, with cook.go) handles values typed unknown and uses them without narrowing (about 965 of the 7,642). Emit the narrowing (typeof / Array.isArray / instanceof on a const, or a typed parameter where the caller's type is known) before each use; the written bytes and every refusal stay exactly as they are. Bring this group's findings to zero.

