# checkJs strict: the message batch code (~500 findings, one of them a real always-true compare)

Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. Card schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types (branch sprint/schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types.w1.g1.e21, head 2b130c5e3) brought `tsc --checkJs --strict` over the generated JS corpus from 41,066 findings to 7,642 with JSDoc only; its report (NOT DONE 1) names the groups that remain, all needing real code changes. Card name of the whole: schema-js-checkjs-strict-to-zero, split into one card per group plus a last card that sets the gate's ratchet to 0. This card is one group. Real code changes in the JS emitter and the runtimes it emits are allowed. THE HARD RULE: the wire bytes stay byte-identical.

THE TASK. The emitted message batch code has four classes of finding (about 511 of the 7,642): (1) `r` used as possibly null after a `count < 0` branch (228); (2) bigint clamp literals typed against number (154); (3) a skip shape with no Element (70); (4) messageRides (internal/codegen/jstable/messagebatch.go:495, used at :545) compares a struct to 0, which is ALWAYS TRUE (59): a real defect of the elision condition. Fix (1) to (3) in the emitted code and its JSDoc. For (4), read docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (read) on the message form's default elision and emit the compare the rule names for a struct field; this may change which fields ride in a batch, so it MAY change message-batch bytes: if it does, do NOT ship that change here: keep the bytes, type the compare honestly so tsc no longer reports it, and report the defect with the Go oracle's answer for the same input as a proposed card (the wire rule holds in this card). Bring this group's findings to zero.

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel(), no real time: TestJsMessageBatchTypesCheck in internal/codegen/jstable/checkjsmessagebatch_test.go, pure Go over the in-process generated JavaScript text of the corpus units (as jsdoctypes_test.go does): every emitted message batch function is free of the four classes: no use of r after count < 0 without a check, every clamp literal typed as the field's numeric type, every skip shape carries Element, and messageRides emits no struct-to-0 compare. REVERSED WITNESS in the same file: undo the fix in a t.TempDir() copy of one generated unit (a planted text edit of the emitted output) and show the check goes red naming the function; record the tsc line the plant brings back.

THE WIRE PROOF (required, in the report): (1) the cross-port conformance corpus: run `make conformance` with SCHEMA_SKIP_LEGS naming every leg except go and js (read the leg list in the Makefile; grep -n conformance Makefile make/*.mk) at BASE_SHA and at head, both green on the js column; (2) a byte diff of encoded outputs: for every fixture the js conformance leg (and the js bench drivers) ENCODE, keep the encoded bytes at BASE_SHA and at head in two directories inside the job and `cmp`/`diff -r` them; the count of files compared and ZERO differences go in the report. A difference in any encoded byte is a defect of this card, never a test to update.

