# checkJs strict: the variable runtime reads descriptor values with no type guard (~3,700 findings)

Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. Card schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types (branch sprint/schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types.w1.g1.e21, head 2b130c5e3) brought `tsc --checkJs --strict` over the generated JS corpus from 41,066 findings to 7,642 with JSDoc only; its report (NOT DONE 1) names the groups that remain, all needing real code changes. Card name of the whole: schema-js-checkjs-strict-to-zero, split into one card per group plus a last card that sets the gate's ratchet to 0. This card is one group. Real code changes in the JS emitter and the runtimes it emits are allowed. THE HARD RULE: the wire bytes stay byte-identical.

THE TASK. The emitted variable runtime (internal/codegen/jstable/variableruntime.go, with variableform.go and variablearms.go) reads `v[fd.n]` per descriptor shape with no typeof / Array.isArray / instanceof guard, so tsc --strict sees an untyped value at each use (about 3,700 of the 7,642; by module the *Variable units hold 6,226). Emit the narrowing tsc understands at each read: a typeof, Array.isArray or instanceof test on a const before the use, or a typed accessor per shape that returns the narrowed type, so the value used is typed without a cast. Where the guard's else branch is reachable on a well-formed value it must do exactly what the code does today (the same read, the same refusal, the same bytes); where it is unreachable it refuses by the existing named refusal. Bring this group's findings to zero.

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel(), no real time: TestJsVariableRuntimeGuardsEveryRead in internal/codegen/jstable/checkjsvariableguards_test.go, pure Go over the in-process generated JavaScript text of the corpus units (as jsdoctypes_test.go does): every descriptor-shaped read in the emitted variable runtime is preceded by a guard tsc narrows on (or goes through a typed accessor), and no emitted read of v[fd.n] is used untyped. REVERSED WITNESS in the same file: undo the fix in a t.TempDir() copy of one generated unit (a planted text edit of the emitted output) and show the check goes red naming the function; record the tsc line the plant brings back.

THE WIRE PROOF (required, in the report): (1) the cross-port conformance corpus: run `make conformance` with SCHEMA_SKIP_LEGS naming every leg except go and js (read the leg list in the Makefile; grep -n conformance Makefile make/*.mk) at BASE_SHA and at head, both green on the js column; (2) a byte diff of encoded outputs: for every fixture the js conformance leg (and the js bench drivers) ENCODE, keep the encoded bytes at BASE_SHA and at head in two directories inside the job and `cmp`/`diff -r` them; the count of files compared and ZERO differences go in the report. A difference in any encoded byte is a defect of this card, never a test to update.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/jstable/ -run '^TestJsVariableRuntimeGuardsEveryRead$' -v` RUNs and PASSes at head (red at BASE); THE COUNT: after each emitter change, regenerate (the repository's make targets for the JS trees and build/tables-generated-js, as make/js.mk names them) and rerun tsc over the corpus the checkjs gate reads (generated/js, generated/js-ludicrous, generated/bench/js, generated/bench/paired/js, build/tables-generated-js) with `--checkJs --strict --noEmit --allowJs` and TypeScript 5.9.3; keep the count by TS code at BASE_SHA and at head in the report. The findings of this group (the variable runtime's untyped reads in *Variable modules) are ZERO at head. THE WIRE PROOF shows zero differences; `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/jstable/ ./internal/codegen/js/ ./internal/goldens/ ./internal/ci/` is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE (schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types reported 5 compiler reds at BASE 8ea510762: TestMapCarriers, TestMapRefusalNamesTheCarrier, TestOptionalArraysCarriers, TestUnionArraysCarriers, TestWasRowsCarriers).

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Record BASE_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD). Export GOFLAGS='-mod=readonly -p=4' NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
