# The JS emitters write no JSDoc types: `tsc --checkJs --strict` reports 41,066 findings on the generated corpus, most of them TS7006

Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19: with the checkjs gate in place, `tsc --checkJs --strict` over the generated JavaScript corpus reports 41,082 findings today, including 36,708 TS7006 (a parameter implicitly has an `any` type). The fix belongs in the emitters, never in suppressions.

THE TASK. (1) The jstable and js emitters write JSDoc types: an `@param` with its type for every parameter of every generated function and method, an `@returns` with its type for every return, and an `@typedef` for the tuple returns (the `[value, ok]` pairs) so the destructuring is typed, plus `@type` on fields and module-level variables where tsc cannot infer them. Types come from the schema (u8..u32 and floats as number, 64-bit as the type the codec already uses (bigint or number: whichever the emitted code holds), string, Uint8Array for bytes, the generated class for a message, Array and Map of the element types for arrays and maps, nullable as the type or null where the sentinel is null); do not use `any`, `*` or `Object` to quiet a finding. (2) Two code fixes ride along, each with its own assertion: drop the unused 4th `stage` argument from the calls and the signature at internal/codegen/jstable/fixedmodule.go:455 and :468 (every caller and the declaration; the generated bytes do not change); and keep narrowing on `[v, ok]` returns, i.e. the emitted code checks `ok` before using `v`, in a form tsc narrows (a destructured const tested in an if, or a typedef'd discriminated tuple), not a cast. (3) Work down the finding classes from the count: after each emitter change, rerun the gate's tsc line and keep the count by TS code in the report (TS7006 first, then the rest). This card is JSDoc-only: the count at head is at or below 7,642 with zero TS7006; it does not chase the remaining classes. (4) If this card touches the checkjs gate's pinned ratchet, it only lowers it to the head count (never raises it); the gate's planted-pattern control stays and still fails the gate. (5) The emitted JavaScript behaviour does not change: the generated tree at BASE and at head, with comment lines starting `/**`, ` *` and ` */` filtered out and the dropped argument accounted for, is identical; say how you checked. Regenerate the JS trees with the repository's make targets and commit what they write under generated/; after merging the base tip, rerun the IsCurrent-style tests on the merged tree.

THE TESTS, each opening with t.Parallel(), no real time:
- TestJsEmitterWritesJsdocTypes, internal/codegen/jstable/jsdoctypes_test.go: pure Go over the generated JavaScript text of the corpus units: every generated function and method has an `@param` for each of its parameters (by name, in order) and an `@returns` unless it returns nothing, every tuple return has its `@typedef`, no type is `any`, `*` or `Object`, and the 4th `stage` argument is gone. Red at BASE.
- The tsc proof, a functional test run by the gate's make target: `tsc --checkJs --strict` over the generated corpus reports at most 7,642 findings and zero TS7006 at head, and the BASE count (41,066) at BASE.
- REVERSED WITNESS, in the same Go test file: drop one `@param` from one generated function (a planted text edit of the emitted output in a t.TempDir() copy) and show both TestJsEmitterWritesJsdocTypes's check goes red naming the function and the tsc line reports a TS7006 at that site (record the tsc line). Check every helper's returned error (internal/ci TestGeneratedHelperResultsAreChecked).

DONE-WHEN: JSDoc-only; tsc --checkJs --strict findings over the generated corpus at or below 7,642 (from 41,066), zero TS7006, no behaviour change (the comment-stripped tree diff shows only the FixedDecode stage-arg fix). In commands: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/jstable/ -run '^TestJsEmitterWritesJsdocTypes$' -v` RUNs and PASSes at head (red at BASE); the gate's tsc line at head reports at most 7,642 findings and zero TS7006 (the BASE count 41,066 and the by-code table at BASE and head are in the report); the reversed witness goes red; `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/codegen/jstable/ ./internal/codegen/js/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/` is green or its only reds are named as present at BASE; the filtered generated-tree diff is empty apart from the dropped stage argument.
