# JavaScript Node/Deno/browser-engine differential (js port of schema)

THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: a differential run of the generated JS conformance tests on Node, Deno and a headless browser engine, checking BigInt and number semantics agree and that every port-level result is identical over the generated js output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Heavy: nightly only.

Files you may touch: the PATHS above, plus the NEW files the card needs (the card's own make file make/schema-js-engine-differential.mk (the Makefile includes make/*.mk, but on this BASE the port registry has not landed, so every make/*.mk stem is probed as a --lang port: when `grep -c '^SCHEMA_PORTS :=' Makefile` prints 0, apply the Makefile hunk of the landed port-list commit 6f993bea byte-identical (`git show 6f993bea -- Makefile | git apply`) and make no other Makefile edit), its own workflow .github/workflows/schema-js-engine-differential.yml (a schedule and workflow_dispatch trigger for nightly parts, push or pull_request for fast parts), and test files; cards share no workflow edits and no Makefile edit beyond that byte-identical hunk, so they land independently. When the work needs a file outside PATHS (the port's test tree, generator, fixtures, saved corpus), report PATHS-PROPOSED with the paths and stop that part as not-done). Do not add needs on other cards: this lens stands alone. Worktree: the staged checkout JOB.md names; branch: the card's own; base: sprint/schema-js.
Libraries considered: the Go standard library and the repository's own tools (tools/negativecontrols, tools/slowgatescan, internal/ci) for gates and tests; the checker or fuzzer named above for the analysis itself, installed fleet-wide from its official source; no hand-written reimplementation of any checker.

DONE-WHEN: the Makefile target exists and passes on the corpus at the card's head; every real finding is fixed with a test that was red at BASE (the failing lines kept); every suppression has a justification; the planted-bad-pattern test is red when the plant is in and green when it is out; CI stays inside its one-minute budget (heavy parts are nightly); the report lists the triage table (finding, REAL or NOT, action) and the other ports' generators that share a flagged pattern.

STEP 1. Enter your worktree with cd <worktree path> && git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac, and never run the heavy tool on the studio.
