# nightly fuzzing (rust port of schema)

NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the rust port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: cargo-fuzz (libFuzzer). Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Use cargo +nightly fuzz with one fuzz_target per reader kind.

Files you may touch: the PATHS above, plus the NEW files the card needs (the card's own make file make/schema-rust-nightly-fuzz.mk (the Makefile includes make/*.mk, so no Makefile edit is needed), its own workflow .github/workflows/schema-rust-nightly-fuzz.yml (a schedule and workflow_dispatch trigger for nightly parts, push or pull_request for fast parts), and test files; cards share no workflow or Makefile edits so they land independently. When the work needs a file outside PATHS (the port's test tree, generator, fixtures, saved corpus), report PATHS-PROPOSED with the paths and stop that part as not-done). Do not add needs on other cards: this lens stands alone. Worktree: the staged checkout JOB.md names; branch: the card's own; base: sprint/schema-rust.
