STEP 5. PROOF THE GATE FIRES. Plant a reader bug (for example drop a bounds check in a scratch copy of the generated reader, switched on only by the test) (in a scratch copy of the generated output or through a generator switch that only a test turns on), show the fuzzer finds it inside the nightly time budget and the saved input then fails the replay test, and keep the red line. Follow the repo's negative-control convention (make/negative-controls.json, tools/negativecontrols): register the control there.
