# rust port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (rust port of schema)

Denial-of-service hardening for the rust port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>.

Files you may touch: the PATHS above, plus the NEW files the card needs (the card's own make file make/schema-rust-resource-bounds.mk (the Makefile includes make/*.mk, but on this BASE the port registry has not landed, so every make/*.mk stem is probed as a --lang port: when `grep -c '^SCHEMA_PORTS :=' Makefile` prints 0, apply the Makefile hunk of the landed port-list commit 6f993bea byte-identical (`git show 6f993bea -- Makefile | git apply`) and make no other Makefile edit), its own workflow .github/workflows/schema-rust-resource-bounds.yml (a schedule and workflow_dispatch trigger for nightly parts, push or pull_request for fast parts), and test files; cards share no workflow edits and no Makefile edit beyond that byte-identical hunk, so they land independently. When the work needs a file outside PATHS (the port's test tree, generator, fixtures, saved corpus), report PATHS-PROPOSED with the paths and stop that part as not-done). Do not add needs on other cards: this lens stands alone. Worktree: the staged checkout JOB.md names; branch: the card's own; base: sprint/schema-rust.
Libraries considered: the Go standard library and the repository's own tools (tools/negativecontrols, tools/slowgatescan, internal/ci) for gates and tests; the checker or fuzzer named above for the analysis itself, installed fleet-wide from its official source; no hand-written reimplementation of any checker.

DONE-WHEN: the Makefile target exists and passes on the corpus at the card's head; every real finding is fixed with a test that was red at BASE (the failing lines kept); every suppression has a justification; the planted-bad-pattern test is red when the plant is in and green when it is out; CI stays inside its one-minute budget (heavy parts are nightly); the report lists the triage table (finding, REAL or NOT, action) and the other ports' generators that share a flagged pattern.

STEP 1. Enter your worktree with cd <worktree path> && git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac, and never run the heavy tool on the studio.
STEP 1. COUNTER. Build the allocation counter harness first and prove it counts by a planted unbounded allocation.
STEP 2. CASES. One test per hostile shape (huge count, deep nesting, recursion, giant string, many unknown fields), each at the documented factor and depth cap, each failing at BASE if the port is unbounded there (keep the failing lines).
STEP 4. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against sprint/schema-rust, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the diff stat, the tests with what each pins, and what was not done.
STEP 5. End as JOB.md says (docs/SPEC-CARD-CONTRACT.md): where JOB.md ends the card with its pull request, that is the end and there is nothing else to write, the gate's lines in the pull request body; where it asks for RESULT.md, write it in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report). The report starts with Verdict: LAND or Verdict: HOLD on line 1 and Head: <sha> on line 2.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.
No gh, no push: JOB.md's finish does both, from outside the wall. Never merge. Every `go test` gets `-timeout 600s`; every new test opens with `t.Parallel()`.
Unit tests use no real time, no sockets, no network and no outside services: time is an argument and a test clock starts at 1000.0. Fuzzing, analyzers that run for minutes and anything needing the network are functional tier, behind the slow gate (read internal/slowtest), never in a unit test.
Install tools only from official sources and only through the fleet play; never print or store a secret or token.
