# rust port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (rust port of schema)

Make the rust port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card.

