# nightly fuzzing (shared port of schema)

NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the shared port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: a mutation fuzzer feeding every port. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Each mutated input goes through every port, and the verdicts must agree: accept or refuse, the refusal reason, and the decoded value. A disagreement is a finding saved as a regression input in the shared conformance vectors. Reuse the harness of the 12-port random-input differential card (schema-shared-12-port-random-differential) if it has landed; otherwise build the smallest driver and say so.

Files you may touch: the PATHS above, plus the NEW files the card needs (the card's own make file make/schema-shared-differential-fuzz.mk (the Makefile includes make/*.mk, so no Makefile edit is needed), its own workflow .github/workflows/schema-shared-differential-fuzz.yml (a schedule and workflow_dispatch trigger for nightly parts, push or pull_request for fast parts), and test files; cards share no workflow or Makefile edits so they land independently. When the work needs a file outside PATHS (the port's test tree, generator, fixtures, saved corpus), report PATHS-PROPOSED with the paths and stop that part as not-done). Do not add needs on other cards: this lens stands alone. Worktree: the staged checkout JOB.md names; branch: the card's own; base: sprint/schema-shared.
Libraries considered: the Go standard library and the repository's own tools (tools/negativecontrols, tools/slowgatescan, internal/ci) for gates and tests; the checker or fuzzer named above for the analysis itself, installed fleet-wide from its official source; no hand-written reimplementation of any checker.

DONE-WHEN: the Makefile target exists and passes on the corpus at the card's head; every real finding is fixed with a test that was red at BASE (the failing lines kept); every suppression has a justification; the planted-bad-pattern test is red when the plant is in and green when it is out; CI stays inside its one-minute budget (heavy parts are nightly); the report lists the triage table (finding, REAL or NOT, action) and the other ports' generators that share a flagged pattern.

ROUTE NOTE (coordinator, 2026-10-19). Start from the CARRY head: the Go-first generated-reader differential fuzzer is written there and its source review is clear. PATHS now names the conformance harness files it needs (test/conformance/go/main.go, reader_fuzz.go, test/conformance/harness/main.go, textfuzz.go, wirefuzz.go) and the fuzz-vector index; a saved differential failure goes under testdata/wire/tables/fuzz-vectors/schema-shared-differential-fuzz/ (a testdata path, always in PATHS). Attempt 2 held only because no gate ran. This attempt runs on a Linux member, changes no source unless a gate goes red, and runs at the exact head, recording command, exit code and raw log for each: make schema-shared-differential-fuzz-replay; make schema-shared-differential-fuzz-negative-control (mutant search red, saved-witness replay red, fixed replay green); make schema-shared-differential-fuzz (bounded native pass); go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ and go vet on the touched packages; and the BASE comparison for the earlier target mismatch in the same environment. If the load guard defers a step, wait for the load to fall and run it again in this attempt.

