# sprint/schema-shared takes sprint/schema-go: the shared (C, C#, Go) base forward-merge

ROUTE NOTE (coordinator, 2026-10-19; why attempts 3 and 4 held). The same finding twice (r3, w4): the head merged a sprint/schema-go tip that was already stale by finish time, so make generated-current failed on generated/bench/{paired,tables}/go (BenchTable.go, BenchTableTable.go and the Cook files). schema-go lands faster than one attempt, so STEP 4b now re-merges the current tip just before finishing and DONE-WHEN judges generated-current against the sha the report names. The carried head 972c47687 (merges of schema-go f8610854 at 13b43736 and ba0e3802 at 972c4768, plus a211d995 skip-absent-optional-cook-storage) is sound in source: BASE sprint/schema-shared 1b2da66e is its ancestor and merge-tree is clean; it is 13 commits behind the schema-go tip ac4dc34b as of this note, so STEP 4b applies at once. Keep base fix #526 (7207fa18: c, cs and cpp carry optional-over-variable; r1 caught a resolution dropping it). PATHS: the standing forward-merge ruling grants merge-carried files byte-identical to the merged parent; PATHS lists the real 1238 changed files as subdirectory globs (never a bare internal/**), and NEW names the files of the directories new at BASE.

THE TASK. sprint/schema-shared is about 730 commits behind sprint/schema-go (64dc1ddd when carded; GO TIP below is the tip you fetch, at or after it). Merge origin/sprint/schema-go into the base as ONE merge commit on the card branch: git fetch origin, then git merge --no-ff GO TIP. Never a rebase, never a squash, never a force-push. A trial merge on 2026-10-18 left these conflicts (a newer GO TIP may add a few; resolve those by the same rules): .github/workflows/cla.yml, ROADMAP.md, docs/SPEC-TABLES.md, generated/bench/paired/go/BenchTableJson.go, generated/bench/tables/go/BenchTableTableJson.go, internal/check/check.go, internal/check/tables_test.go, internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go, internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, internal/tablenames/js.go. Resolve each conflict keeping BOTH sides' intent, by these rules and no others: shared Go and IR code (ir/, internal/check/, internal/parser/, compiler/, internal/codegen/gotable/, tools/, .github/) takes GO TIP's version; port-specific code keeps the port's version, adapted to the new IR; spec text (docs/*.md) merges both rewrites, each statement true of the merged code; ROADMAP.md is regenerated with make roadmap, never hand-edited; the roadmap sexp ledgers (docs/roadmap.sexp, docs/roadmap-evidence/*.sexp) keep each row's true state at the merge head. The shared files in this list (.github/workflows/cla.yml, generated/bench/paired/go/BenchTableJson.go, generated/bench/tables/go/BenchTableTableJson.go, internal/check/check.go, internal/check/tables_test.go, internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go, internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, internal/tablenames/js.go) take GO TIP's version, then re-add only what the shared (C, C#, Go) base adds that GO TIP lacks. Then regenerate the goldens, the generated trees and the bench the merge leaves stale with the repository's own Makefile targets, and commit the regenerated files in the merge commit or a second commit on the same branch. Nothing else changes: no rule is ported here.

LANDING. The card lands by pushing the merge to the base: the head is the merge commit (plus any regeneration commit), the member pushes the branch, and nova-sprint land brings it onto sprint/schema-shared with the merge commit kept, never squashed or rebased.

DONE-WHEN: git merge-base --is-ancestor GO TIP HEAD is true at head and false at BASE (print both and the GO TIP hash); git log --merges -1 --format=%P HEAD names BASE's tip and GO TIP; the port's unit gate (go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/check/ ./internal/codegen/gotable/ ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./internal/codegen/cstable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/, then make generated-current) passes, with no new reds against the pre-merge BASE except reds that are also red on GO TIP itself, each named and shown red there (TestSpecGoS13S15FollowOnsLanded is one of those). GO TIP is the schema-go sha named in the report, merged by STEP 4b just before finishing; make generated-current is clean against it at head (no stale generated, bench or golden file).

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names and run git log --oneline -1; it is a NEW worktree on the branch this card names. Export GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command; GOCACHE is already set to the machine's shared build cache (JOB.md names it): keep it. Build and test only on the Linux bench JOB.md names, never the working Mac.
STEP 2. Run the gate at BASE first and keep each last line (go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/check/ ./internal/codegen/gotable/ ./internal/codegen/ctable/ ./internal/codegen/cstable/ ./compiler/ ./internal/ci/, then make generated-current): those are the pre-merge reds.
STEP 3. git fetch origin; print GO TIP (git rev-parse origin/sprint/schema-go); git merge --no-ff GO TIP; list the conflicts with git diff --name-only --diff-filter=U and resolve each by the rules in THE TASK. Commit the merge with the trailer.
STEP 4. Regenerate (make roadmap, then each stale golden, generated tree and bench) and run the gate. When a test fails, name its file and say whether it was changed by your resolution (yours), arrived red from schema-go (run it at GO TIP and keep the line), or is unchanged (already red at BASE), and report that line first.
STEP 4b. RE-MERGE AT FINISH (coordinator, 2026-10-19; schema-go moves faster than one attempt). Just before finishing, git fetch origin and merge the CURRENT origin/sprint/schema-go tip again (git merge --no-ff, never a rebase), resolve by the same rules, rerun make generated-current and regenerate and commit what it names, and rerun the gate. The report names the schema-go sha the head last merged (GO TIP below means that sha). A head that merged a tip older than the one current at landing is not a defect when generated-current is clean against the sha it names.
STEP 5. Commit on your own branch with the trailer. Nothing reaches the forge from inside the wall: in the job the git shim records a push, the pull request is the finish JOB.md names (the last STEP), and the member makes both, against the BASE: line's branch, from outside the wall when the card finishes. The pull request body states the merge commit, each conflict and how it was resolved, the diff stat against BASE, the gate lines, and what was not done.
STEP 6. End as JOB.md says; the report starts with Verdict: LAND or Verdict: HOLD on line 1 and Head: <sha> on line 2.")
